ersity property; to help safeguard property of the U.T. System Administration or an institution of The University of Texas System. Responsible ... View Details Bookmark CLINICAL THERAPIST (School of Medicine/Student Affairs) SRGV9009 Ofc of Student Affairs SOM Staff To provide specialized assistance and mental health counseling to the School of Medicine students. Responsible for a variety of professional tasks related to developing, implementing and conducting specialized individual and group psychotherapy in a clinical setting. Uses independent judgment and discretion in diagnosing and formulating clinical treatment plans for clients. View Details Bookmark Part-Time Lecturer Health & Biomedical Sciences (Master of Science in Health Sciences) 2026-2027 PTFRGV1085 College of Health Professions  / Health and Biomedical Sciences Temporary Faculty We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as a part-time lecturer in the Department of Health and Biomedical Sciences beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. About UTRGV: UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond through an innovative, unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leadi... View Details Bookmark SENIOR FINANCIAL AID COORDINATOR SRGV9136 Financial Aid Staff To provide supervisory skills in the coordination of several programs and activities in the day to day operation of the University the Office of Student Financial Services. Responsible for decision making processes requiring initiative and judgment in responding to individual needs of students for administration of one or more programs areas within the office of Student Financial Services, and ... View Details Bookmark PATIENT SERVICES REPRESENTATIVE II ( UT Health RGV Multispecialty - Harlingen) UTHRGV29 School of Medicine / Ambulatory Operations UT Health RGV To coordinate clerical and medical activities of a healthcare team, patient registration activities, and facilitating access to UTRGV services for new and returning patients. To ensure and create a positive patient experience by consistently exceeding expectations in customer services and patient care. To provide high level customer service consistently with both internal and external customers... View Details Bookmark SENIOR FINANCIAL ANALYST SRGV9116 Fin Planning & Reporting SOM Staff To provide supports for executive decision-making by conducting complex financial analysis and preparing and presenting reports in order to optimize resource-allocation at the institution. View Details Bookmark SOFTWARE ENGINEER I / SOFTWARE ENGINEER II SRGV9137 Office of the Provost Academic Affairs Staff SOFTWARE ENGINEER ITo develop fundamental skills including Analysis, Design, Development, and Implementation of the computer-based Information Systems to ensure efficiency, accuracy, and support the business processes of the University, including the Student, Finance, Human Resources (ERP systems) and all associated third party software applications.SOFTWARE ENGINEER IIPerform mid-level analysi... View Details Bookmark IT MEDIA SYSTEMS TECHNICIAN I SRGV9134 Infrastructure & Operations Staff To provide the daily operation, installation, troubleshooting, and maintenance of all assigned IT Media Systems, such as classroom technology systems, videoconferencing technology systems, and digital signage technology systems in support of UTRGV faculty, students, staff and visitors. View Details Bookmark IT APPLICATIONS ADMINISTRATOR II SRGV9121 Infrastructure & Operations Staff Responsible for providing mid-level support and administration for IT applications to ensure that required specifications are implemented. To coordinate installations and upgrades with multiple IT teams and university departments to optimize the effectiveness of the interaction of information systems and organizational processes. View Details Bookmark BUILDING ATTENDANT I - NIGHT SRGV8766 Campus Facilities Operations Staff To perform routine manual work involving the custodial maintenance of buildings. View Details Bookmark INTERNATIONAL STUDENT SERVICES SPECIALIST SRGV9129 Ofc of Intl Student Services Staff To provide support to the International Student Services in the processing of immigration and other related documents needed to facilitate enrollment for undergraduate and graduate international students. View Details Bookmark Clinical Neurologist – Cognitive – Open Rank FRGV2047 School of Medicine / NBHISU Neuroscience Faculty The Department of Neuro and Behavioral Health at the University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) seeks a motivated and energetic candidate for an open rank position in the non-tenure academic clinician track, with expertise in managing and treating various cognitive specific disorders. These disorders may include but, not be limited to Alzheimer’s disease (or other forms of dementia), Mild Co... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Practice (Master Teacher) in the UTRGV UTeach program FRGV2046 College of Sciences / Mathematical and Statistical Sciences Faculty We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as an Assistant Professor of Practice in the UTRGV UTeach program in the College of Sciences, preferably beginning in the Spring 2027 semester. Responsibilities involve teaching and/or supervising undergraduate students in courses and field experiences related to preservice teacher developme... View Details Bookmark TRANSIT SUPERVISOR (UTRGV EMPLOYEES ONLY) SRGV9133 Campus Auxiliary Services Staff To manage the day-to-day operations of campus shuttle services. Responsible to provide transportation services in a safe and timely manner. View Details Bookmark Graduate Teaching Assistant - EECE A1257 College of Engineering and Computer Science / Electrical and Computer Engineering Assistantships Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE). View Details Bookmark Research Assistant - Electrical Engineering A1276 College of Engineering and Computer Science / Electrical and Computer Engineering Assistantships Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters. Maximum appointment may be increased up to forty (40) hours per week (100% FTE) during the summer if funded by a grant. View Details Bookmark OFFICE ASSISTANT SRGV9132 College of Education and P-16 Integration / Bilingual and Literacy Studies Staff To perform clerical duties for a department. Responsible for the performance of clerical, typing and data entry duties. View Details Bookmark Graduate Assistant - OBI A1486 Bilingual Integration Assistantships GA will provide the OBI with assistance in various research activities, View Details Bookmark SENIOR ADMINISTRATIVE ASSOCIATE SRGV9131 Ofc of Health Affairs Staff To provide advanced and complex administrative support to a Vice President or similar level position and assumes considerable responsibility for office management. Responsible for many complex office decisions and administrative support, with minimal direction. View Details Bookmark Center for Latin American Arts (CLAA): Graduate Research Assistant A1493 College of Fine Arts / Art and Design Assistantships This position will be focused on research at the Center for Latin American Arts, specifically assisting the Director of this ORU to plan, explore, organize, and execute projects that support faculty and student research for scholarship, performance, museum studies, and exhibition in the fine arts. This includes helping facilitate collaborations among faculty, students, and the community to prom... View Details Bookmark LABORATORY / TECHNICAL SERVICES SUPERVISOR SRGV9130 College of Health Professions / Nutrition & Dietetics Staff To provide responsible supervisory and technical skills to ensure safe operation of all equipment and to oversee the distribution and maintenance of supplies and equipment in departmental laboratories or related areas and techniques of normally used equipment and materials. View Details Bookmark DIRECTOR, APEX ACCELERATOR SRGV9094 Business Development Staff To manage and oversee the planning, organization and administration of the APEX Accelerator. Responsible for providing senior leadership skills and direction for the daily Operation of the APEX Accelerator Center. View Details Bookmark SCHOOL OF MEDICINE- UNDERGRADUATE MEDICAL EDUCATION CURRICULUM MANAGER SRGV9102 Ofc of Educational Affairs Staff To manage and maintain the educational quality of the Undergraduate Medical Education (UME) program and ensure compliance with the Licensing Committee on Medical Education (LCME) accreditation standards, SOM Central Curriculum Authority Committee (CCAC) guidelines and other regulatory requirements. Responsible for the alignment, implementation and compliance of the LCME standards and managing r... View Details Bookmark ASSISTANT MEN’S AND WOMEN’S TENNIS COACH SRGV9128 Athletics Staff To assist with the daily coaching and recruitment activities of the Men’s and Women’s Tennis teams. Assist the Coach with all areas of the program including but not limited to coaching, film exchange, budget administration and recruiting of prospective student athletes. View Details Bookmark FINANCIAL MANAGER SRGV9127 Office of Research Staff To manage the daily operations and functions of an assigned finance or accounting unit. Responsible for supervising staff assigned to the area and implementing strategic programs to ensure the improvement of the department’s business processes in accordance with the University’s mission and goals. View Details Bookmark Division Chief of Vascular Surgery FRGV1981 School of Medicine / Surgery ISU Faculty The UTRGV School of Medicine Department of Surgery is recruiting a board certified or board eligible vascular surgeon to be core faculty and serve as Division Chief of vascular surgery in the Department of Surgery. Leadership experience in academic vascular surgery is preferred.  Core faculty duties will include direct patient care, scholarly activity, and faculty development.  Active participa... View Details Bookmark WS Graduate Assistant - Degree Progress & Graduation Initiatives A1359 Office of Student Success Assistantships Description of Duties:Provide guidance and support to students seeking assistance from program.May lead or support student success projects related to communication, outreach, data analysis, workshops, academic innovation, presentations, and social media.Develop resources and guides geared at helping students prepare for graduation.Work with student success and academic tools, technology platfo... View Details Bookmark TECHNOLOGY LICENSING ASSOCIATE SRGV9125 Technology Commercialization Staff To provide the intake, review, management, and licensing of intellectual property created at UTRGV. Responsible for working closely with industrial counterparts, faculty, and patent attorneys for development, licensing, and commercialization of new technologies created at UTRGV. View Details Bookmark INSTITUTIONAL TITLE IX AND EQUAL OPPORTUNITY INVESTIGATOR / SENIOR INSTITUTIONAL TITLE IX AND EQUAL OPPORTUNITY INVESTIGATOR SRGV9052 Title IX & Equal Opportunity Staff INSTITUTIONAL TITLE IX AND EQUAL OPPORTUNITY INVESTIGATOR:Supports the Chief Equal Opportunity & Title IX Officer at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley by performing fact-gathering and investigative functions primarily related to discrimination, equal opportunity, sexual misconduct, and retaliation complaints by employees, students, and others protected under state or federal civil r... View Details Bookmark INFORMATION SECURITY ANALYST SRGV9120 Information Security Staff Responsible for assisting with the development, implementation, monitoring and support of digital access control, data confidentiality, system integrity, system reliability, system audit, recovery methods and procedures. Ensures the university is in compliance with UT System policies as well as state and federal statutes and regulations. View Details Bookmark Go to search results page: Previous 1 2 3 4 5 6 Next The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley UT System Employee Benefits UT System Fraud Reporting State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal Where the money goes To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
