    "https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "University of Texas-Rio Grande Valley: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:careers.utrgv.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs University of Texas-Rio Grande Valley: All Jobs 2026-08-13T15:10:37-05:00 https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52207 2026-08-13T15:10:37-05:00 2026-08-13T15:10:37-05:00 Teaching Assistant_Informatics & Engineering Systems <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Informatics & Engineering Systems https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51830 2026-07-16T10:27:34-05:00 2026-07-16T10:27:34-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Mechanical Engineering <div>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions, as well as a commitment to UTRGV’s strategic priorities (<a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/mvv/index.htm\"><strong>Mission, Vision, and Core Values | UTRGV</strong></a>), which include promoting access to postsecondary education to a diverse student body and to become one of the largest and most successful Hispanic-serving emerging research institutions in the U.S.A.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Mechanical Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52401 2026-08-31T15:56:29-05:00 2026-08-31T15:56:30-05:00 INFORMATION SECURITY ANALYST <div>Responsible for assisting with the development, implementation, monitoring and support of digital access control, data confidentiality, system integrity, system reliability, system audit, recovery methods and procedures. Ensures the university is in compliance with UT System policies as well as state and federal statutes and regulations.</div> Information Security https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51155 2026-05-14T17:35:56-05:00 2026-05-14T17:35:56-05:00 Part-time Lecturer- School of Nursing <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a <em>Part-Time Faculty </em>of the School of Nursing beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. The assignment is semester to semester basis.<br><br>The School of Nursing at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley occasionally has the need to hire non-tenure track Part- Time Lecturer(s) to teach in its Bachelor’s and/or Master’s programs. Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction to students in the classroom, simulated laboratories, and clinical settings<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div><div><br><strong>Department/College Background<br></strong>The School of Nursing offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Nursing. These degrees include a traditional BSN and 2nd degree BSN pre-licensure degree, an RN to BSN, along with graduate degrees in Family Nurse Practitioner, a Post-graduate certificate in Psychiatric Mental Health NP and our new Doctor in Nursing Practice (DNP) that started in Fall 2022. Our faculty teach on two campuses, in both Edinburg and in Brownsville. We have full simulation labs that offer state of the art educational opportunities for all our students. We collaborate with the other health science programs at UTRGV on interdisciplinary clinical experiences and work with hospitals throughout the entire Rio Grande Valley. UTRGV is committed to preparing its students to succeed, and seeks faculty who are prepared to help in this goal.</div><div><br></div> School of Nursing https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50627 2026-03-26T16:40:38-05:00 2026-03-26T16:40:39-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Bilingual & Literacy Studies <div><em>“The Department of Bilingual and Literacy Studies at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) occasionally has the need to hire non-tenure track, part-time Lecturers to teach in undergraduate Bilingual Education and Reading courses for the Fall, Spring and/or Summer Semesters. Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction within the program.”</em><br><br><strong><br>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div><br></div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Bilingual and Literacy Studies https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52117 2026-08-05T16:55:13-05:00 2026-08-05T16:55:13-05:00 HVACR SUPERVISOR <div>Provides highly advanced (senior level) skills necessary to perform heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and refrigeration (HVACR) repair and maintenance of mechanical equipment. Responsible for managing and supervising a department that oversees all air conditioning and related mechanical equipment and utility systems. Works under minimal supervision with extensive latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment.</div> Campus Facilities Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52438 2026-09-02T16:18:33-05:00 2026-09-02T16:18:34-05:00 Assistant Professor of Practice (Master Teacher) in the UTRGV UTeach program <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as an Assistant Professor of Practice in the UTRGV UTeach program in the College of Sciences, preferably beginning in the Spring 2027 semester. Responsibilities involve teaching and/or supervising undergraduate students in courses and field experiences related to preservice teacher development. Primary responsibilities include teaching field-based courses which students take in their pursuit of teacher certification, working with local area public school administrators who accept students for field experiences, working with local area public school teachers who serve as mentors for the students, and conducting field observations of the students. Additional duties include student mentoring, induction support, and other program related tasks and service activities. The position is for a three-year appointment, renewable based on performance.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being.&nbsp; The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UTRGV UTeach is a middle and high school mathematics and science teacher preparation and certification program that promotes inquiry-based learning and instruction. We prepare highly skilled, inspiring educators with deep subject expertise through integrated and cohesive coursework with early and consistent community-based teaching experiences. UTRGV UTeach is one of the largest UTeach programs in the nation, and as of December 2025, we have produced 550 highly prepared STEM graduates, an estimated 90% of whom entered the teaching profession.</div> College of Sciences / Mathematical and Statistical Sciences https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51688 2026-06-30T14:55:47-05:00 2026-06-30T14:55:47-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant for Rehabilitation Services & Counseling 2026-2027 <div>Graduate Assistant will assist Research Faculty with the research needs of the project.</div> College of Health Professions  / Rehabilitation Services and Counseling https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52293 2026-08-20T13:28:48-05:00 2026-08-20T13:28:49-05:00 ENROLLMENT SPECIALIST <div>To provide support in the assigned area within U Central and provide routine support and assistance to students and other visitors with Enrollment Services, including but not limited to admissions, registration, and financial aid. Responsible for assisting students in successfully completing enrollment service applications, documentation, and transactions. Responsible for interpreting rules, regulations, and procedures/policies to students, parents, and outside agencies.</div> Student Service Centers https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51162 2026-05-15T08:51:02-05:00 2026-05-15T08:51:03-05:00 Orthopedic Surgeon (Open Rank) <div>The UTRGV SOM seeks a Board-Certified Orthopedic Surgeon to expand our specialty practice and be Core Faculty in a developing Orthopedic Residency. Candidates with Orthopedic fellowship training in Adult Reconstruction/ Joint Replacement, Hand Surgery, Orthopedic Foot &amp; Ankle or Sports Medicine are preferred.<br><br></div><div>As a Core Faculty member, selected candidate will participate in direct patient care, scholarly activity, faculty development, patient safety and quality improvement initiatives, prepare and provide didactics, participate in the evaluation of the residents &amp; the program, and prepare for and participate in ACGME and other accreditation and non-accreditation site visits. As faculty, they will also administer and maintain a professional educational environment conducive to educating residents in each of the ACGME competencies and in assisting them to reach their individual Milestones. Academic rank and title will be awarded commensurate with academic qualifications and certification.</div><div><strong><br></strong><br></div> School of Medicine / Surgical Specialty and MSK ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52211 2026-08-13T15:32:31-05:00 2026-08-13T15:32:32-05:00 PhD - Research Assistant - Computer Science <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Computer Science https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51853 2026-07-17T15:31:34-05:00 2026-07-17T15:31:35-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Medical Education (Health System Science) <div>The Department of Medical Education at the UTRGV School Of Medicine (UTRGV SOM) in Edinburg, TX seeks a highly qualiﬁed faculty member to lead and teach Health System Science primarily within the pre-clerkship curricular years of the MD program. The candidate will develop and manage the module during the pre-clerkship curriculum. This is a wonderful opportunity for an outstanding academic Health System Scientist who is enthusiastic about teaching and education, to contribute to a young medical school with an extremely dynamic environment.</div><div>Candidates should have a desire and ﬂexibility to integrate instruction across other disciplines within a fully integrated curriculum. All candidates with an enthusiasm for teaching and those with prior teaching experience in a health profession related environment are encouraged to apply; however, prior teaching experience in an LCME-accredited medical school would be considered preferred. This position will be responsible for teaching, developing, and implementing Health System Science in medical school curriculum which encompasses key areas related to healthcare, systems thinking, epidemiology, quality improvement in healthcare, patient safety, social determinants of health, population health, global health, statistics and health policy. This position has a full-time instructional mandate, and the recruited candidate must be committed to excellence in the teaching and mentoring of ﬁrst- and second-year medical students, in addition to teaching within other graduate programs offered by the School of Medicine. The present MD curriculum at the school is of a hybrid nature, designed around the Problem Based Learning (PBL) modality, while also employing traditional lecture-based instruction.</div><div><br><br></div> School of Medicine / Medical Education ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52403 2026-08-31T16:32:18-05:00 2026-08-31T16:32:19-05:00 TECHNOLOGY LICENSING ASSOCIATE <div>To provide the intake, review, management, and licensing of intellectual property created at UTRGV. Responsible for working closely with industrial counterparts, faculty, and patent attorneys for development, licensing, and commercialization of new technologies created at UTRGV.</div> Technology Commercialization https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50681 2026-04-01T10:18:26-05:00 2026-04-01T10:18:26-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Registrar <div>Office of the Registrar is looking for Graduate students seeking a part-time position to provide support and assistance.<br><br></div><ul><li>Provides support to faculty, staff and students and performs duties as assigned.</li><li>Assists with complex tasks and imaging related to record keeping and documentation.</li><li>Organizes communications and written materials to increase department efficiency.</li><li>Assists with special projects, assigned office tasks, preparation of communications, and planning and execution of events.</li><li>Provides specialized support that requires computer skills, data entry accuracy and software savviness.</li><li>Performs other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Registrar https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52128 2026-08-07T10:21:16-05:00 2026-08-07T10:21:17-05:00 DIGITAL SCHOLARSHIP LIBRARIAN <div>Leads the development of digital initiatives and research data management projects that support scholarly communication at UTRGV and explores new opportunities for the library's support of faculty research.</div> University Library https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52442 2026-09-03T11:03:29-05:00 2026-09-03T11:03:29-05:00 INTERNATIONAL STUDENT SERVICES SPECIALIST <div>To provide support to the International Student Services in the processing of immigration and other related documents needed to facilitate enrollment for undergraduate and graduate international students.</div> Ofc of Intl Student Services https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51691 2026-06-30T15:03:06-05:00 2026-06-30T15:03:07-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant for Occupational Therapy 2026-2027 <div><em>Research Assistants are hired to assist faculty in carrying out specific aspects of an individual faculty member’s research agenda.</em></div><ol><li>Conduct literature reviews</li><li>Generate annotated bibliography</li><li>Complete scoping/ systematic review</li><li>Collect data and analyze data for current projects</li><li>Prepare materials for IRB review</li><li>Prepare qualitative interview questions</li><li>Prepare Qualtrics/quantitative surveys for administration</li><li>Recruit and/or interview subjects</li><li>Maintain accurate records of interviews, safeguarding the confidentiality of subjects, as necessary</li><li>Summarize and transcribe interviews</li><li>Provide ready access to all experimental data for the faculty researcher and/or supervisor</li><li>Request or acquire equipment or supplies necessary for the project</li><li>Manage and respond to project related email (as applicable)</li><li>Prepare, maintain, and update website materials (as applicable)</li><li>Attend all project meetings</li><li>Attend area seminars and other meetings as necessary</li><li>Summarize project results in manuscript format for publication</li><li>Prepare progress reports for the PI and funding agency</li><li>Prepare other articles, reports, and presentations</li><li>Present oral presentation or poster presentation</li></ol> College of Health Professions / Occupational Therapy https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52321 2026-08-21T16:15:32-05:00 2026-08-21T16:15:33-05:00 Research Assistant - Center for Nanotechnology <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters. Maximum appointment may be increased up to forty (40) hours per week (100% FTE) during the summer if funded by a grant.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Mechanical Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51233 2026-05-22T10:17:21-05:00 2026-05-22T10:17:21-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant / Marine Ecosystems Institute <div>Research Assistants will be assigned to assist a faculty member with data collection, analyzation, publication of data, and other duties as assigned.</div> Marine Ecosystems Institute https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52235 2026-08-17T10:03:11-05:00 2026-08-17T10:03:11-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Graduate College <div>This position manages a range of social media activities, including content development, graphic design, and coordinating online posts and stories.</div> Graduate College https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/49093 2025-10-22T10:48:11-05:00 2025-10-22T10:48:12-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor (Open Rank) - Electrical & Computer Engineering <div>The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) at the University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) seeks applicants for three (3) faculty positions in the broad area of Electrical Engineering. The department will consider all qualified candidates; however, preference will be given to candidates who can enhance the department's electrical and computer engineering capabilities in areas such as, but not limited to, electric power and energy systems, telecommunications, digital communications, and applied artificial intelligence (AI)<strong>. </strong>Successful candidates are expected to start in the Fall 2026 semester.<br><br>The ECE department at UTRGV has an enrollment of over 900 undergraduate students in the ABET-accredited BSEE and BSCE undergraduate programs and 36 master's students in the MSE program. Successful candidates are expected to show a strong commitment to teaching excellence, mentoring students at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and conducting research and publishing scholarly materials at the two main campuses where the ECE department is located. UTRGV is moving towards being Carnegie Classified as an R1 university soon, and faculty being considered for these positions will be evaluated on their ability to support this effort. The College of Engineering &amp; Computer Science has an interdisciplinary PhD program in Materials Science and Engineering and several centers in which the successful candidate can participate as appropriate: the Center for Advanced Manufacturing Innovation and Cyber Systems (CAMICS), the Center for Nanotechnology, the Center for Multidisciplinary Research Excellence in Cyber-Physical Infrastructure Systems (MECIS), the University Transportation Center for Railway Safety (UTCRS), and the Industrial Training and Assessment Center. Please visit our website at <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/cecs/departments/ece/\"><strong>www.utrgv.edu/ece/</strong></a>.</div><div><br>The positions are for tenure-track assistant professors; however, exceptional candidates may be considered for credit toward time on the tenure track or for appointment as associate professor.</div><div><em><br><br></em><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.<br>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.<br>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Electrical and Computer Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51931 2026-07-23T10:28:42-05:00 2026-07-23T10:28:43-05:00 Graduate Assistant Instructor <div>Graduate assistant Instructor will be the Instructor of Record and responsible for teaching the courses assigned by the department/school Graduate Coordinator (example: POLS 2305 and/or POLS 2306).</div> College of Liberal Arts / Sch of Pol Sci Pub Af Lg & Sec https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52411 2026-09-01T10:07:43-05:00 2026-09-01T10:07:44-05:00 Division Chief of Vascular Surgery <div>The UTRGV School of Medicine Department of Surgery is recruiting a board certified or board eligible vascular surgeon to be core faculty and serve as Division Chief of vascular surgery in the Department of Surgery. Leadership experience in academic vascular surgery is preferred.&nbsp; Core faculty duties will include direct patient care, scholarly activity, and faculty development.&nbsp; Active participation in the education of undergraduate medical students and graduate medical education programs is required. The successful candidate will participate in all aspects vascular surgery and endovascular therapy. The candidate will play a vital role in the growth and development of vascular surgery care in the Rio Grande Valley.<br><br></div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Lead and grow a vascular division encompassing collaborations with the School of Podiatric Medicine at UTRGV and partnering hospitals in the Rio Grande Valley</li><li>Drive clinical program development and regional referral growth aligned with UTRGV priorities.</li><li>Advance a sustainable research enterprise, including clinical trials, translational research, and extramural funding</li><li>Recruit, mentor, and retain faculty, fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration, and academic advancement</li><li>Partner with departmental and institutional leadership to strengthen education, innovation, and multidisciplinary vascular care.</li></ul> School of Medicine / Surgery ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52339 2026-08-25T10:02:19-05:00 2026-08-25T10:02:20-05:00 SUPERVISING CLINICAL THERAPIST <div>To provide specialized assistance and counseling to the general community population. Responsible for a variety of professional tasks related to developing, implementing and conducting specialized individual and group psychotherapy in a clinical setting.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Counseling Training Clinic https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50792 2026-04-13T10:14:19-05:00 2026-04-13T10:14:19-05:00 Academic Child/Adolescent Psychiatrist <div>The UTRGV School of Medicine seeks a child/ adolescent psychiatrist to join our growing faculty for the undergraduate and graduate medical education program, including residencies in General and Child &amp; Adolescent Psychiatry located in Harlingen, TX. Responsibilities include direct patient care, program development, resident supervision, medical student teaching, and scholarly activities. Faculty will participate in creating and implementing the educational and clinical training sites of the developing Medical School.<br><br>The UTRGV SOM has a residency program in psychiatry and will be adding child/adolescent psychiatry fellowship. These programs are conceptualized as being natural extensions of the medical school experience with the goals of providing both general and specialized didactic and clinical experiences to produce well rounded, skilled psychiatrists and child/ adolescent psychiatrists who can work with a range of problems and types of populations in diverse settings. The mission of these programs is to graduate skilled, compassionate, versatile physicians who are knowledgeable about systems of care, diverse ethnic and cultural populations, and collaborative care in addition to being knowledgeable and competent in the general clinical practice of psychiatry and child/ adolescent psychiatry. The residency training programs will emphasize inpatient and, psychotherapy, integrated experiences with primary care, multidisciplinary teaching, multiple community sites and a cohesive, integrated approach to learning, understanding and utilizing the science of medicine for effective psychiatric practice. Experiential activities will be supported by an interconnected didactic and clinical curriculum that emphasizes self-initiated learning, problem solving skills, and appropriate use of technology. Faculty will be actively involved in teaching residents in a variety of forums with the expectation that faculty and trainees will work closely together. Faculty and residents will also work with medical students and trainees from other specialties.<br><br>Faculty joining these residency programs will have the opportunity to develop and start educational, clinical and research programs within a system that prioritizes working within the community, incorporating prevention and early intervention into care, and collaboration within and outside of medicine. While the primary focus of these positions will be the development of clinical and educational programs, teaching and supervising trainees and the provision of direct clinical care, applicants with current or prior research experience and interest are also encouraged to apply. Protected time for scholarly activities and/or start-up research support can be provided based on interest, prior experience and future career goals.</div> School of Medicine / NBHISU Psych Neuro & Optometry https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52131 2026-08-07T12:54:10-05:00 2026-08-07T12:54:11-05:00 NURSE PRACTITIONER / PHYSICIAN ASSISTANT <div>Nurse Practitioner:<br>Works under moderate supervision of a physician to provide advanced practice nursing care and treatment within primary care and/or board recognized specialization.<br><br>Physician Assistant:<br>To provide primary health care services in a clinical setting under the supervision and direction of a primary care physician in one of the following areas: adult health and/or adolescent health. Responsible for the performance of tasks of a standardized nature which are complex and require considerable experience of specialized training, but which do not constitute the practice of medicine.</div> School of Medicine / Ambulatory Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52448 2026-09-03T14:19:36-05:00 2026-09-03T14:19:37-05:00 IT APPLICATIONS ADMINISTRATOR II <div>Responsible for providing mid-level support and administration for IT applications to ensure that required specifications are implemented. To coordinate installations and upgrades with multiple IT teams and university departments to optimize the effectiveness of the interaction of information systems and organizational processes.</div> Infrastructure & Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51720 2026-07-06T00:19:04-05:00 2026-07-06T00:19:05-05:00 Lecturer Health and Human Performance CoHP 2027-2028 3 yr (Kinesiology Teacher Certification) <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a <strong><em>Lecturer </em></strong>within <strong><em>The Department of Health and Human Performance </em></strong><em>(HHP) </em>beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year. This is an in-person position of instruction with a home base campus (Edinburg).</div><div><br><strong><em>About UTRGV:</em></strong></div><div><br>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div><br>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div><br>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students.&nbsp;</div><div><br><strong><em>Department/College Background</em></strong></div><div><br></div><div>The <strong><em>Department of Health &amp; Human Performance </em></strong>in the <strong><em>College of Health Professions </em></strong>is seeking qualified candidates who have a demonstrated record of success in teaching and professional service that are commensurate with an appointment as Lecturer to begin fall 2027. The position is a nine-month, non-tenured faculty position. The position requires teaching undergraduate courses in kinesiology or exercise science, serving as a field supervisor for practicums, serving as a student academic advisor, service on university, college, and departmental committees and taskforces, community engagement, service in the profession, and performing other duties assigned by the department chair. Given that UTRGV is a distributed campus, faculty will be required to teach in various settings, incorporating technology and student-engaged pedagogies to maximize student success, and may be assigned to teach face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online courses. Service to the department, college, university, community, and professional organizations is integral to the faculty member’s responsibilities.</div><div><br>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college and program mission and be committed to UTRGV’s guiding principles, which include promoting access to postsecondary education to a diverse student body and to become one of the largest and most successful Hispanic-serving emerging research institutions in the U.S.A.</div><div><br>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as a Lecturer in the College of Health Professions beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year.</div><div><br><strong><em>College Information</em></strong></div><div><br></div><div>The College of Health Professions is the leading institution of excellence in health and human services, education, health care and research. Our main goal is to produce highly skilled practitioners, educators, and researchers through our 23 high quality educational programs. Students who are accepted into our programs enter into an educational environment, which through student centered, meaningful experiential learning opportunities, results in the development of new scientific and intellectual inquiry for the promotion of health equity in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond.</div><div><br>The College houses one school, seven departments, the Border Health Office and other health centers and organizations that are focused on improving the health of our South Texas Community. In the College of Health Professions at UTRGV, we are dedicated to training the next generation of health professionals and leaders to fill the roles of practitioner, educator and researcher in the 21st Century.</div><div><br><strong><em>Our Vision</em></strong></div><div><br></div><div>We envision the College of Health Professions as a world-class institution committed to achieving the highest quality of life and health equity through education, research, and engagement with our communities.</div><div><br><strong><em>Our Mission</em></strong></div><div><br></div><div>The College of Health Professions will be the leading institution of excellence in health and human services, education, health care and research, producing highly skilled practitioners, educators, and researchers through high-quality educational programs, meaningful experiential learning opportunities and the development of scientific and intellectual inquiry for the promotion of health equity in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond.</div><div><br></div> College of Health Professions / Health and Human Performance https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51284 2026-05-29T16:58:05-05:00 2026-05-29T16:58:06-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Informatics & Engineering Systems <div>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions, as well as a commitment to UTRGV’s guiding principles (<a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/introduction/\"><strong>https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/introduction</strong></a>), which include promoting access to postsecondary education to a diverse student body and to become one of the largest and most successful Hispanic-serving emerging research institutions in the U.S.A.<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Informatics & Engineering Systems https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52241 2026-08-17T12:38:11-05:00 2026-08-17T12:38:11-05:00 WS - Graduate Research Assistant in Manufacturing & Industrial Engineering <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Manufacturing and Industrial Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/49304 2025-11-07T14:49:41-06:00 2025-11-07T14:49:41-06:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Computer Science <div>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions, as well as a commitment to UTRGV’s strategic priorities (<a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/mvv/index.htm\"><strong>Mission, Vision, and Core Values | UTRGV</strong></a>), which include promoting access to postsecondary education to a diverse student body and to become one of the largest and most successful Hispanic-serving emerging research institutions in the U.S.A.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Computer Science https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51988 2026-07-28T13:11:51-05:00 2026-07-28T13:11:52-05:00 DIRECTOR, FINANCIAL PLANNING AND REPORTING, SOM <div>To provide leadership and oversight for strategic financial planning, financial reporting and budgetary planning and processes across the School of Medicine.</div> Fin Planning & Reporting SOM https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52413 2026-09-01T10:13:49-05:00 2026-09-01T10:13:50-05:00 ASSISTANT MEN’S AND WOMEN’S TENNIS COACH <div>To assist with the daily coaching and recruitment activities of the Men’s and Women's Tennis teams. Assist the Coach with all areas of the program including but not limited to coaching, film exchange, budget administration and recruiting of prospective student athletes.</div> Athletics https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51753 2026-07-08T12:26:50-05:00 2026-07-08T12:26:51-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Civil Engineering <div>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions, as well as a commitment to UTRGV’s strategic priorities (<a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/mvv/index.htm\"><strong>Mission, Vision, and Core Values | UTRGV</strong></a>), which include promoting access to postsecondary education to a diverse student body and to become one of the largest and most successful Hispanic-serving emerging research institutions in the U.S.A.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Civil Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52358 2026-08-25T17:07:45-05:00 2026-08-25T17:07:45-05:00 UNIVERSITY POLICE OFFICER IV <div>To enforce the law, provide service, information and aid to all citizens as circumstances require, prevent crime, suppress disturbances, investigate criminal offenses, and arrest offenders. Serves as a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). Responsible for enforcement duties for the protection, safety and welfare of students, employees, visitors, and all property within the area under the control and jurisdiction of The University of Texas System. Exercises independent judgment within the limits prescribed by law, Rules and Regulations of the Board of Regents, institutional rules and regulations and Director of Police departmental policies and procedures.</div> University Police https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50824 2026-04-15T09:49:13-05:00 2026-04-15T09:49:13-05:00 Assistant Professor of Psychiatry <div>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley School of Medicine Department of Neuro and Behavioral Health seeks an Adult General Psychiatrist for inpatient and outpatient services. The selected candidate will provide high-quality clinical care and clinical teaching. In addition, they will participate in scholarly activity, faculty development, patient safety and quality improvement initiatives, prepare and provide didactics, and participate in the evaluation of the residents and medical students. While previous experience in a residency program teaching role is preferred, individuals just finishing residency/fellowship training are highly encouraged to apply. Faculty are expected to administer and maintain a professional educational environment conducive to educating residents in each of the ACGME competencies, assisting them to reach their individual Milestones, plus educating medical students in the practice of Psychiatry. Working within the UT Health RGV clinical mission, the Department has outstanding educational and scholarly activities for medical students and a growing Psychiatry program. Demonstration of strong commitment to the education of residents and medical students is essential. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishments and experience.<br><br></div> School of Medicine / NBHISU Psych Neuro & Optometry https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52133 2026-08-07T13:05:53-05:00 2026-08-07T13:05:54-05:00 Graduate Assistant - School of Medicine VMD <div>| • Assist in the preparation of budgets, grant requests, class schedules and other periodic reports.<br>• Assist in processing various student forms and requests for the appropriate review and approvals.<br>• Assist in planning and facilitation of applicant interviews and tours. • Provides general program information and materials to students and/or direct students to the appropriate student services resources.<br>• Assist in coordination, planning, and/or staffing of departmental meetings and events as needed for outreach, recruitment &amp; education.<br>• Reviews discrepancy reports and analyzes student records to identify errors, determine their source, and make corrections. (Analyzes admissions/enrollment data as directed)<br>• Monitors complex records and prepares reports from a variety of materials.<br>• Collects information from a wide variety of sources.</div> Ofc of Student Affairs SOM https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52451 2026-09-03T17:15:39-05:00 2026-09-03T17:15:40-05:00 SOFTWARE ENGINEER I / SOFTWARE ENGINEER II <div><strong>SOFTWARE ENGINEER I</strong><br>To develop fundamental skills including Analysis, Design, Development, and Implementation of the computer-based Information Systems to ensure efficiency, accuracy, and support the business processes of the University, including the Student, Finance, Human Resources (ERP systems) and all associated third party software applications.<br><br><strong>SOFTWARE ENGINEER II</strong><br>Perform mid-level analysis, design, development, and implementation for the computer-based Information Systems to ensure efficiency, accuracy, and support the business processes of the University, including the Student, Finance, Human Resources (ERP systems) and all associated third party software applications.</div> Office of the Provost Academic Affairs https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52423 2026-09-01T17:20:32-05:00 2026-09-01T17:20:32-05:00 DIRECTOR, APEX ACCELERATOR <div>To manage and oversee the planning, organization and administration of the APEX Accelerator. Responsible for providing senior leadership skills and direction for the daily Operation of the APEX Accelerator Center.</div> Business Development https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51375 2026-06-07T19:50:37-05:00 2026-06-07T19:50:37-05:00 Chair of Medicine and Oncology <div>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) School of Medicine invites applications for the position of <strong>Chair of the Department of Medicine and Oncology</strong>. This leader will set the department’s strategic vision, guide faculty development, and oversee all academic, clinical, and operational functions. The Chair reports directly to the Dean of the School of Medicine.</div><div><br><strong>Position Overview</strong></div><div>The Chair of Medicine and Oncology will lead the continued growth of an academic department dedicated to advancing cancer prevention, innovative research, and exceptional medical education. A central focus of the department is the development of a comprehensive academic oncology program addressing cancers prevalent in the Rio Grande Valley. The program integrates clinical services, translational research, clinical trials, and education within the Cancer and Surgery Center.</div><div>The Chair is responsible for providing visionary leadership and ensuring excellence across all departmental missions, including:</div><ul><li><strong>Clinical Leadership:</strong> Oversight of high quality patient care within all departmental clinical programs.</li><li><strong>Research Advancement:</strong> Support and growth of basic, translational, and clinical research initiatives, including clinical trials.</li><li><strong>Education:</strong> Integration of outstanding educational programs for medical students, residents, fellows, and other trainees.</li><li><strong>Faculty Development:</strong> Recruitment, mentorship, evaluation, and promotion of faculty; fostering a culture of wellness, collaboration, and professional growth.</li><li><strong>Administration:</strong> Financial oversight, budget planning, and resource allocation aligned with institutional priorities.</li><li><strong>Strategic Planning:</strong> Development and implementation of departmental strategies consistent with the School of Medicine’s mission.</li><li><strong>Representation:</strong> Serve as an ambassador for the department at local, regional, state, and national levels.</li></ul><div><strong>Additional Responsibilities (UTRGV School of Medicine Standard Expectations for Chairs)</strong></div><div>The Department Chair shall:</div><ul><li>Report directly to the Dean</li><li>Ensure effective administration of the department</li><li>Lead regular department meetings to communicate key updates, policies, and programmatic initiatives</li><li>Recruit and recommend appointments of faculty, including community faculty</li><li>Oversee implementation of all UTRGV and SOM policies applicable to the department</li><li>Develop and submit the department’s annual budget, including compensation recommendations</li><li>Manage departmental finances and space allocation</li><li>Recommend faculty appointments, promotions, and tenure</li><li>Organize the department to meet current and emerging needs of the School of Medicine</li><li>Ensure faculty wellness, mentorship, career development, and performance evaluation</li></ul> School of Medicine / MDOISU Oncology https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52244 2026-08-17T15:07:27-05:00 2026-08-17T15:07:28-05:00 BUILDING ATTENDANT FOREMAN - NIGHT <div>To perform supervisory work in leading custodial maintenance staff in performing cleaning assignments.<br><br>Responsible for leading, assigning, and scheduling work assignments to custodial maintenance staff who perform cleaning assignments throughout campus.</div> Campus Facilities Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/49809 2026-01-05T16:04:37-06:00 2026-01-05T16:04:37-06:00 Medical Hematologist/Oncologist <div>Provide clinical expertise in patient care management and an appropriate teaching environment for fellows, residents, and students. Practice clinical cancer medicine in an exemplary manner in standards set forth by the Texas State Board of Medical Examiners, and the American College of Physicians, properly balanced with other academic activities. Must be capable of providing complete and thorough history and physical patient examinations. Must be able to perform invasive procedures as dictated by the physician’s subspecialty. This may require standing, bending, stooping, lifting, hearing, manual dexterity, and clear and concise verbal communications.<br><br></div><div>Develop and maintain a clinical practice for patients referred to UT Health RGV. Provide physician staffing for the out-patient clinic and in-patient services at a level commensurate with that which would be provided by other Oncology staff/internists with the same level of training and experience. Serve as a role model practitioner for faculty, fellows, residents, and students.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Actively engage in clinical research and scholarly activities to enhance the academic environment. Develop programs of clinical research and scholarly activities as assigned. May necessitate instructing, through written or verbal communication, research support personnel in protocol implementation. Seek appropriate funding mechanisms to support clinical research.&nbsp;<br><br></div> School of Medicine / MDOISU Oncology https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51999 2026-07-29T10:42:49-05:00 2026-07-29T10:42:50-05:00 BILLING CLERK <div>Responsible for conducting patient registration, insurance verification, scanning, printing, and posting payments and adjustments in the Electronic Medical Records (EMR) system.</div> School of Medicine/ Revenue Cycle https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51768 2026-07-09T16:18:04-05:00 2026-07-09T16:18:05-05:00 ASSOCIATE DEAN FOR RESEARCH <div>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) School of Medicine seeks a dynamic and visionary Associate Dean for Research to serve as a senior academic leader responsible for advancing and integrating the school’s research mission. Reporting to the Dean, the Associate Dean will provide strategic leadership across the full continuum of biomedical research—from basic discovery to clinical application to population health impact.</div><div>This role is ideally suited for a clinician–scientist with broad experience spanning clinical medicine, basic and translational research, clinical trials, and population health research. The Associate Dean for Research will play a defining role in shaping the next phase of the UTRGV School of Medicine’s research enterprise. By integrating discovery with patient care, cancer research across the continuum, maternal health, and population health, this leader will ensure that scientific advances translate into meaningful improvements in outcomes, equity, and community well-being. Through mentorship, collaboration, and strategic alignment, the Associate Dean will help position UTRGV School of Medicine as a nationally recognized institution for impactful, mission-driven research that improves lives across generations.</div><div>The successful candidate will foster a strong culture of scholarship, mentorship, and innovation while aligning research growth with the School of Medicine’s clinical mission and the health priorities of the Rio Grande Valley.</div> School of Medicine / Research SOM https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52364 2026-08-26T11:04:06-05:00 2026-08-26T11:04:06-05:00 POLICE COMMUNICATIONS OPERATOR <div>The primary function of a Police Telecommunicator is to receive and prioritize Emergency 9-1-1 and non-emergency telephone calls from the public. Enters information into a Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) system, and processes non-emergency and routine requests for police and security services. Dispatch appropriate emergency services such as police, fire and emergency medical services. Monitors public safety units in the field. Retrieves computer data for emergency response personnel within the service area. The Police Telecommunicator may provide alarm and closed circuit television monitoring services while performing multiple tasks concurrently in a fast paced environment maintaining a professional and positive demeanor. Serves as a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). Impacts law enforcement and security efforts of UTPD.</div> University Police https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50849 2026-04-17T10:56:44-05:00 2026-04-17T10:56:44-05:00 Research Assistant in Manufacturing & Industrial Engineering <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Manufacturing and Industrial Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52150 2026-08-11T08:25:45-05:00 2026-08-11T08:25:45-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Medical Education - Physiology <div><br>The UTRGV School of Medicine seeks a faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor for teaching Physiology. Teaching of pre-clerkship physiology and related topics; didactic lectures, lab sessions, PBL, resources sessions, office hours for student mentoring; administration; other duties as required. Additionally, the desire and ﬂexibility to integrate instruction across other disciplines within a fully integrated curriculum, along with the ability to work collegially within an interdisciplinary team of other clinical/basic science educators would be considered an asset. The chosen individual will assist in implementing a vertically and horizontally integrated curriculum utilizing active learning, team-based learning, problem-based learning, flipped classroom and self-directed study. This position has a full-time instructional mandate, and the recruited candidate must be committed to excellence in the teaching and mentoring of ﬁrst- and second-year medical students.</div><div><br><br></div> School of Medicine / Medical Education ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52458 2026-09-04T11:59:40-05:00 2026-09-04T11:59:40-05:00 SENIOR FINANCIAL AID COORDINATOR <div>To provide supervisory skills in the coordination of several programs and activities in the day to day operation of the University the Office of Student Financial Services. Responsible for decision making processes requiring initiative and judgment in responding to individual needs of students for administration of one or more programs areas within the office of Student Financial Services, and for the development of information and repost as required by financial aid programs.</div> Financial Aid https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52428 2026-09-02T09:37:44-05:00 2026-09-02T09:37:44-05:00 Center for Latin American Arts (CLAA): Graduate Research Assistant <div>This position will be focused on research at the Center for Latin American Arts, specifically assisting the Director of this ORU to plan, explore, organize, and execute projects that support faculty and student research for scholarship, performance, museum studies, and exhibition in the fine arts. This includes helping facilitate collaborations among faculty, students, and the community to promote the arts and provide support with researching content for new projects that are funded by winning CLAA grants. With work based at the CLAA, this Graduate Research Assistant will help this ORU in the College of Fine Arts maintain its <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/claa/index.htm\"><strong>CLAA mission statement</strong></a>to facilitate the exchange of ideas among students, faculty, artists, and scholars to bring creative academic projects to our university and share them with the Rio Grande Valley community, audiences in Texas, and participants beyond in international venues especially Latin America.</div> College of Fine Arts / Art and Design https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51481 2026-06-12T16:50:20-05:00 2026-06-12T16:50:21-05:00 Open Rank - Clinical Asst/Assoc/Professor Faculty Positions Physical Therapy CoHP 2026-2027 3yr <div>The Department of Physical Therapy at the University of Texas Rio Grande Valley is inviting applications for a full-time faculty in the CAPTE Candidate Doctoral Physical Therapy Program. This is an open rank, clinical-track solicitation. Faculty rank and salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications and based on established university and department standards. The start date for the position is 1 September 2026. The position may fall under either a nine-month contract with part-time summer employment available, or a nine-plus-three contract with full time summer employment.</div><div><br>The successful candidate will: teach courses in their area of expertise; advise and mentor physical therapy students; participate in university, professional and community service; and engage in scholarship. Additionally, the successful candidate will have demonstrated knowledge and expertise in one or more of the following physical therapy areas: pediatrics, adult neurological management, geriatrics, pelvic floor rehabilitation, acute care, cardiopulmonary rehabilitation, health and wellness, or management of chronic health conditions.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div><div><strong>Department/CollegeBackground</strong></div><div><br>The College of Health Professions (CoHP) at UTRGV includes seven health professions departments with 11 undergraduate, twelve graduate and three doctoral degree programs. The CoHP and programmatic faculty work closely with the UTRGV School of Medicine, School of Podiatric Medicine, School of Nursing and the UT Health System to provide robust interprofessional education opportunities and training experiences for health professions students.</div><div><br>The Department of Physical Therapy is housed in a 55,000 sq ft facility in Harlingen, Texas. The department is currently completing renovations for a state-of-the-art facility that will include three large classrooms, two large teaching laboratories, an anatomy suite with cadaveric and dry-lab teaching areas, three core research labs and ample office and student-centric learning spaces. Beginning in 2027, the building will be shared with the Department of Occupational Therapy who will have independent, state-of-the-art teaching, and research spaces. The DPT program is a nine-semester (three-year), full-time face-to-face program and is accepting its second cohort in the summer of 2026. The program serves a unique role in the PT profession in general and the Rio Grande Valley specifically to improve access to and quality of physical therapy services to rural and medically underserved areas in South Texas through education, research and community engagement and outreach.</div> College of Health Professions/Physical Therapy https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52249 2026-08-18T10:35:24-05:00 2026-08-18T10:35:24-05:00 Research Assistant in Mechanical Engineering <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters. Maximum appointment may be increased up to forty (40) hours per week (100% FTE) during the summer if funded by a grant.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Mechanical Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/49974 2026-01-15T15:21:35-06:00 2026-01-15T15:21:35-06:00 Graduate Research Assistant - CSRPA <div>The GRA principal duty is to contribute to a program of survey research and analysis. Assisting in the collection and analysis of data with responsibilities mostly related to those undertaken by The Center for Survey Research &amp; Policy Analysis [CSRPA]. May also be assigned to different undergoing projects, and assist with clerical duties related to these research projects.&nbsp;</div> College of Liberal Arts / Sch of Pol Sci Pub Af Lg & Sec https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52026 2026-07-29T16:53:07-05:00 2026-07-29T16:53:07-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Human Development & School Services <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as a Part-Time Lecturer for the Department of Human Development and School Services in the <strong>2026-2027</strong>&nbsp;academic year.<br><br>The Department of Human Development &amp; School Services at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) occasionally has the need to hire non-tenure track, part-time Lecturers to teach in its Bachelor’s/ Master’s/Doctoral Special Education, School Psychology, Educational Psychology, and Early Childhood programs beginning in the Fall, Spring and/or Summer semesters. Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction within the program.<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Human Development and School Services https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51792 2026-07-13T15:03:01-05:00 2026-07-13T15:03:02-05:00 Academic Biochemist (Assistant Professor) <div>The UTRGV School of Medicine seeks a faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor for teaching Biochemistry, molecular biology and genetics. Experience teaching in an LCME accredited medical school is preferred. The chosen individual will assist in implementing a vertically and horizontally integrated curriculum utilizing active, team based, and problem based learning, flipped classroom and self-directed study.<br><br></div><div><br><br></div> School of Medicine / Medical Education ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52380 2026-08-28T08:58:04-05:00 2026-08-28T08:58:05-05:00 Part-Time Clinical Assistant Professor Physician Assistant CoHP 2026-2027 <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a <em>Part-Time</em> <em>Clinical Assistant Professor </em>of the <em>Department of Physician Assistant </em>beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year.</div><div><br></div><div>Duties and Responsibilities:<br><br></div><div>· Provide student instruction and teach courses (didactic and/or clinical) as assigned by the&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Program Director/Department Chair.</div><div>· Supervise students in didactic and/or clinical courses and activities.</div><div>· Provide direct clinical instruction to PA students during supervised patient care experiences.</div><div>· Assist with the development, implementation, and evaluation of student performance.</div><div>· Perform other program and department level duties, as assigned.</div><div><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div><br>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div><br>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div><br>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> College of Health Professions / Physician Assistant https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51049 2026-05-05T09:09:36-05:00 2026-05-05T09:09:36-05:00 Assistant Professor - Family Medicine without OB <div>The Department of Primary &amp; Community Care, Division of Primary &amp; Preventive Care, is seeking a full time Physician for a medical school affiliated Family Medicine clinical practice located in the Rio Grande Valley. The faculty member is expected to maintain an outpatient clinical practice that may include supervision of residents and advanced practitioners and teaching of medical students. Academic rank will be awarded commensurate with academic experience and credentials.<br><br></div> School of Medicine / Primary and Community Care ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52173 2026-08-12T13:53:22-05:00 2026-08-12T13:53:22-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Assistant Coach Football <ol><li>Assist the Head Coach with practice and game-day preparation and execution.</li><li>Maintain and ensure student-athlete academic integrity.</li><li>Provide service to the Institution as assigned by the Director of Athletics &amp; Recreation or the Head Coach.</li><li>Adhere to NCAA, conference, departmental, and university policies, procedures, and expectations.</li><li>Assists with the identification, recruitment and selection of quality student-athletes and maintains contact with prospective student-athletes</li><li>Serves as liaison between sport supervisor including facilities, marketing and promotions, game operations, ticket and media relations</li><li>Assists with the development of marketing strategies for recruiting prospective student-athletes and community engagement.</li><li>Assists with alumni and community relations and outreach.</li><li>Manages all logistics of team travel and coordinates, organizes, and collaborates with vendors regarding team travel, meal arrangements, and team practice sites.</li><li>Organizes and maintains accurate inventory of volleyball equipment and uniforms.</li><li>Oversees marketing, outreach and administrative duties for camp activities</li><li>Demonstrate knowledge, understanding, and commitment to University, NCAA, and WAC compliance rules and regulations</li><li>Assist with the organization and planning of practice and competitive strategies.</li><li>Performs other duties as needed.</li></ol><div><br></div> Athletics https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52462 2026-09-04T16:06:52-05:00 2026-09-04T16:06:54-05:00 CLINICAL THERAPIST (School of Medicine/Student Affairs) <div>To provide specialized assistance and mental health counseling to the School of Medicine students. Responsible for a variety of professional tasks related to developing, implementing and conducting specialized individual and group psychotherapy in a clinical setting. Uses independent judgment and discretion in diagnosing and formulating clinical treatment plans for clients.</div> Ofc of Student Affairs SOM https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52099 2026-08-05T13:36:07-05:00 2026-08-05T13:36:07-05:00 Assistant/Associate/Professor of Neurology - Neurophysiology and Epilepsy <div>The Department of Neurology and Behavioral Health at the University of Texas Rio Grande Valley School of Medicine seeks a motivated and energetic candidate for an Assistant Professor position in the non-tenure academic clinician track, with expertise in managing and treating various seizure disorders, including but not limited to focal and generalized seizures, as well as autoimmune and hereditary epilepsies. The candidate should be comfortable reading infant, pediatric, and adult EEGs, and take a leadership role in developing the Epilepsy program and establishing a research center by collaborating with the UTRGV Research Department.<br><br>Responsibilities will include teaching UTRGV School of Medicine students and residents (Neurology, Internal Medicine, Family Medicine, and Podiatry).<br><br>The successful candidate will have no inpatient hospital responsibilities. The outpatient clinic is located at the Institute of Neuroscience in Harlingen, Texas.</div> School of Medicine / Surgical Specialty and MSK ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52430 2026-09-02T11:51:26-05:00 2026-09-02T11:51:26-05:00 Graduate Assistant - OBI <div>GA will provide the OBI with assistance in various research activities,</div> Bilingual Integration https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51573 2026-06-24T12:33:42-05:00 2026-06-24T12:33:43-05:00 Part Time Lecturer School of Rehabilitation Services & Counseling COHP 2026-2027 <div>Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction and possible clinical supervision in the school.<br><br>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to scholarly work, student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions, and are committed to UTRGV’s strategic plan, vision, mission, values and core priorities. (https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/).</div> College of Health Professions  / Rehabilitation Services and Counseling https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52264 2026-08-18T16:22:05-05:00 2026-08-18T16:22:07-05:00 COMMUNITY HEALTH WORKER (UT Health RGV AHEC Primary Care (La Victoria) <div>Responsible for providing outreach education services within the scope of a given project in order to meet Research Center for Minority Institutions (RCMI) program requirements. Serve as a health advocate and provide basic information regarding clinic and community services to promote clinic services and encourage visits.</div> School of Medicine / Primary and Community Care ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50080 2026-01-27T10:47:38-06:00 2026-01-27T10:47:38-06:00 Research Assistant in Materials Science and Additive Manufacturing <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters. Maximum appointment may be increased up to forty (40) hours per week (100% FTE) during the summer if funded by a grant.<br><br>Dr. Ahsan’s Lab in the Department of Manufacturing and Industrial Engineering at UTRGV will be immediately recruiting a motivated graduate (master’s/PhD) student to start as early as Summer 2026. The selected candidate will work on a funded research project focused on developing novel alloys for energy applications in harsh environments using additive manufacturing. This research involves integrating computational modeling, machine learning, and experimental investigations to design and characterize new alloys and composites fabricated via laser powder bed fusion additive manufacturing. This work is closely woven into materials science, additive manufacturing, and machine learning realm, with applications in energy and extreme environments. The candidate will receive a monthly stipend and tuition support.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Manufacturing and Industrial Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51811 2026-07-14T13:39:47-05:00 2026-07-14T13:39:47-05:00 Graduate Assistant - UTRGV Psychology Clinic <div>The UTRGV Psychology Clinic is seeking a qualified graduate assistant to join our mental health clinic team during the summer semester, providing high‑quality mental health services and clinical training experiences for graduate students. We serve a diverse population with a strong emphasis on culturally responsive care for disadvantaged communities, supported by practicum training and research opportunities across mental and behavioral health disciplines. Our staff, faculty, and students frequently work bilingually in English and Spanish through collaboration with local agencies, and the ideal candidate will be highly organized, academically strong, and motivated to gain hands‑on experience in clinical operations, data analysis, research support, and community engagement.<br><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities<br></strong><br></div><div>• Assist with office management, including processing referrals, screening clients, and checking in clients using electronic health records.<br>• Distribute outcome measures and assist with data entry, organization, and analysis.<br>• Analyze clinic outcomes data and develop statistical reports.<br>• Assist with managing clinic training materials and didactic content.<br>• Provide support to social media outreach and wellness campaigns.<br>• Conduct literature searches using library and online research tools.<br>• Support research activities, including methodology design and literature review development.<br>• Co-author research papers with faculty when applicable.<br>• Assist faculty with teaching materials and grading assignments.<br><br></div><div><strong>Learning Objectives<br></strong><br></div><div>During the assistantship, the graduate assistant will learn to:<br>• Identify common mental health concerns through client screening and assessment.<br>• Assess and monitor mental health outcomes for research and treatment evaluation.<br>• Demonstrate proficiency in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and research-related data software.<br>• Understand management and coordination of mental health services and assist with social media outreach efforts.<br>• Develop and maintain procedures for assessing clinical outcomes and making data-informed decisions.<br>• Communicate effectively with clinic staff, faculty, and students through professional written and oral communication.<br>• Apply critical thinking and problem-solving skills to clinic operations and research tasks.<br>• Generate recommendations to enhance service quality and workflow efficiency.<br>• Demonstrate cultural humility and professionalism in working with diverse communities and multidisciplinary teams.<br>• Exhibit ethical conduct, responsibility, and professionalism in all interactions.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Psychological Science https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52393 2026-08-31T11:02:19-05:00 2026-08-31T11:02:19-05:00 ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT FOR STRATEGIC BUSINESS AFFAIRS <div>Reports directly to the Executive Vice President for Finance and Business Affairs and Chief Financial Officer and serves as the principal advisor on strategic business affairs, enterprise contract administration, administrative governance, and institutional business process strategy. Provides executive leadership for enterprise initiatives that strengthen operational effectiveness, standardize administrative practices, improve internal controls, and advance the University's strategic priorities.<br><br>The Associate Vice President serves as the University's executive business owner for contract administration and leads cross-functional efforts to modernize business operations, improve service delivery, and promote operational excellence across academic and administrative divisions. The position collaborates extensively with University leadership to align business operations with institutional priorities while respecting the independent authority of other executive offices. The AVP coordinates with the Office of Legal Affairs on matters requiring legal review or legal interpretation but does not provide legal advice, establish legal positions for the University, or perform the functions of University Counsel.<br><br></div> Finance & Business Affairs https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51080 2026-05-07T09:08:10-05:00 2026-05-07T09:08:10-05:00 Graduate Assistant Instructor- Literatures & Cultural Studies <div>Graduate Assistant Instructor will be the Instructor of Record and<br>responsible for teaching the courses assigned by the department<br>graduate coordinator.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Literatures and Cultural Studies https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52190 2026-08-13T09:34:24-05:00 2026-08-13T09:34:25-05:00 POSTDOCTORAL FELLOW <div>We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Fellow to join a two-year research project funded through a USDA-APHIS New World Screwworm (NWS) Grand Challenge grant. The successful candidate will work closely with the Principal Investigators (PIs) to develop and implement innovative research integrating machine learning, computer vision, and wildlife monitoring applications. Under limited supervision, the Postdoctoral Fellow will collaborate with the PIs to design and conduct field- and modeling-based research. In this position the Fellow will: Develop, train, and evaluate machine learning models for image processing and automated detection of animal infestations, wounds, and other indicators of susceptibility to myiasis; and apply computer vision approaches using imagery collected from drone-mounted cameras and other high-resolution imaging platforms to support the early detection of infestations in wildlife populations. This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to cutting-edge research at the intersection of artificial intelligence, wildlife health, and biosecurity while working within a collaborative, multidisciplinary team.</div> College of Sciences/ Ctr VectrBrne Zoontc Emgng Dis https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50193 2026-02-09T13:45:05-06:00 2026-02-09T13:45:06-06:00 Part Time Lecturer in the Robert C. Vackar College of Business and Entrepreneurship/Information Systems <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a Part Time Lecturer in the Department of Information Systems<em> </em>beginning in Fall 2026.<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.<br><br></div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.<br><br></div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> RCV College of Business and Entrepreneurship / Information Systems https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52110 2026-08-05T15:22:36-05:00 2026-08-05T15:22:37-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant for Health Sciences 2026-2027 <div>Dr. Batholomew Chireh at the Department of Health Sciences, University of Texas Rio Grande Valley, on the Edinburg Campus, invites applications for a part-time contract Graduate Research Assistant position. The successful applicant will be involved in various research projects, but I will expect most of his/her work will be dedicated towards a pilot study assessing ergonomic risk factors and heat exposure as determinants of musculoskeletal disorders and mental wellbeing among port personnel in the Rio Grande Valley.</div> College of Health Professions/Health Sciences https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52433 2026-09-02T15:21:20-05:00 2026-09-02T15:21:20-05:00 Research Assistant - Electrical Engineering <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters. Maximum appointment may be increased up to forty (40) hours per week (100% FTE) during the summer if funded by a grant.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Electrical and Computer Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51661 2026-06-30T08:52:35-05:00 2026-06-30T08:52:36-05:00 Open Rank Clinical Assistant/Clinical Associate Professor-Master of Sciences in Health Science - Health & Biomedical Sciences 2027-2028 3 yr <div>The Department of Health and Biomedical Sciences at the University of Texas Rio Grande Valley is inviting applications for a full-time faculty position in the Master of Science in Health Science (MSHS) Program. This is an open-rank, clinical-track solicitation. Faculty rank and salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications and will be based on established university and department standards. The start date for the position is September 1, 2027. The position will be a nine-month contract, with the potential for summer teaching opportunities.</div><div><br>The successful candidate will complete the required training to teach online, design and implement curriculum for graduate-level health science courses, participate in university, professional, and community service, and engage in scholarship. All faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college, department, and program missions, as well as a commitment to UTRGV’s strategic plan, vision, mission, values, and core priorities. (https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/).</div><div><br></div><div><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div><br>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond through an innovative, unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div><br>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building on our strengths in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advances in research and creative work, expanding access to high-quality, affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div><br>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit the <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div><div><br><strong>Department/College Background</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The College of Health Professions (CoHP) at UTRGV includes ten health professions departments and offers 11 undergraduate, 12 graduate, and 3 doctoral degree programs. The CoHP and programmatic faculty work closely with the UTRGV School of Medicine, School of Podiatric Medicine, School of Nursing, and the UT Health System to provide robust interprofessional education opportunities and training experiences for health professions students.</div><div><br>The Department of Health and Biomedical Sciences is housed on both the Brownsville and Edinburg UTRGV campuses. The MSHS program is an Accelerated Online Program (AOP) offered in a completely online, asynchronous format. The program serves a diverse student population and offers a unique interdisciplinary approach to health sciences graduate education.</div> College of Health Professions  / Health and Biomedical Sciences https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52272 2026-08-19T09:53:21-05:00 2026-08-19T09:53:22-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Philosophy <div>The Graduate Assistant will provide programmatic, and research support to the Department of Philosophy's Master of Science in Bioethics program. Responsibilities may include assisting with student recruitment and outreach activities, maintaining program records, supporting online and in-person events, conducting literature reviews and research related to bioethics topics, assisting with grant-related activities, preparing reports and program materials, and supporting faculty initiatives associated with the MS in Bioethics program. The Graduate Assistant will work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students while contributing to the growth, promotion, and daily operations of the Bioethics program.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Philosophy https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52201 2026-08-13T11:56:07-05:00 2026-08-13T11:56:07-05:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant (Sociology) <div>Duties include, but are not limited to, providing feedback and/or grading student work; monitoring/proctoring course activities; leading laboratory sessions, discussion sessions, or recitation labs; providing office hour assistance to students; and performing clerical tasks associated with course instruction. Additional details provided by Department.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Sociology https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51824 2026-07-15T15:55:04-05:00 2026-07-17T10:42:52-05:00 Medical Director, Diabetes Center of Excellence (Endocrinologist or Diabetologist- Open Rank) <div>Lead the strategic development of the UTRGV Diabetes Center of Excellence, with a focus on innovation, collaboration, and high-impact outcomes. Provide clinical expertise in Endocrinology in a multidisciplinary care setting. Teaching, mentoring, and providing an appropriate research environment for medical students, residents, fellows, and other trainees. Collaborate with leadership across medicine, nursing, pharmacy, podiatry, and other health professions to design integrated, team-based care models that address prevention, education, and treatment of diabetes and its complications. We expect this individual to champion access to care tailored to the needs of the Rio Grande Valley population. Actively participate in and champion value-based care initiatives and population health programs focused on diabetes management and outcomes. In partnership with operational leadership, develop quality metrics, clinical pathways, and oversee data dashboards to ensure excellence in clinical outcomes, patient satisfaction, and adherence to ADA standards of care. This individual is expected to participate in quality improvement and accreditation efforts.<br><br>Serve on or attend institutional committee meetings as assigned. Assume administrative duties as assigned. Present, participate, and attend teaching and continuing education conferences. Present lectures using visual aids to medical students, residents, fellows, and other trainees. Support faculty development efforts related to diabetes prevention and management.<br><br>Actively engage in clinical research and scholarly activity to enhance the academic environment. Develop and maintain independent clinical research programs as appropriate, which may necessitate (orally or in writing) instructing research support personnel in protocol implementation. Collaborate with other investigators. Write manuscripts describing scientific developments based on research projects for publication in peer-review journals. Seek and obtain appropriate funding mechanisms to support clinical research, if necessary. May require completion of grant proposals, applications, budget development, and analysis.<br><br><br><br>Oversee the design and growth of clinical programs including population health initiatives, high-risk patient care coordination, digital health integration, and chronic care management services. Develop and maintain a clinical endocrinology practice for UT Health RGV. Visually view, evaluate, and interpret medical records, physical exams, and other relevant data of patients; to include competency in taking history and examining patients. Process all essential clinical and diagnostic findings into sound treatment recommendations in multidisciplinary settings. Ensure all quality control standards are implemented and constant quality assurance measures are in place. Must be self-motivated, conscientious, and able to communicate (orally and in writing) and relate well to peers and personnel at the technical and administrative level.<br><br><br></div> School of Medicine / Medicine and Oncology ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52400 2026-08-31T15:31:21-05:00 2026-08-31T15:31:21-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant - Institute for Advanced Manufacturing <div>Research Assistant will assist Research Faculty with the research needs of the project.</div> Institute for AdvManufacturing https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51087 2026-05-07T10:18:26-05:00 2026-05-07T10:18:26-05:00 Radiation Oncology (Open Rank) <div>The UTRGV SOM is seeking a Board Certified or Board Eligible physician in Radiation Oncology to provide both clinical (non-teaching) and academic radiation services. Clinical responsibilities will include outpatient radiation services and may include in-patient consultation. Academic responsibilities may include teaching residents/medical students in the outpatient clinical setting and in the classroom. Participation in scholarly activity, faculty development, patient safety and quality improvement initiatives, and other administrative and program committees are expected. Also, preparation and presentation of program didactics, grand rounds, and assisting with undergraduate medical education will be assigned at the Chair's discretion. The successful candidate will develop a robust clinical/translational research program that advances the therapeutic paradigm.<br><br></div><div><br></div><div>Academic rank will be awarded commensurate with academic experience and credentials.<br><br></div> School of Medicine / MDOISU Medicine https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50239 2026-02-12T16:24:41-06:00 2026-02-12T16:24:41-06:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant (Sociology) <div>Duties include, but are not limited to, providing feedback and/or grading student work; monitoring/proctoring course activities; leading laboratory sessions, discussion sessions, or recitation labs; providing office hour assistance to students; and performing clerical tasks associated with course instruction. Additional details provided by Department.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Sociology https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52116 2026-08-05T16:53:46-05:00 2026-08-05T16:53:46-05:00 GROUNDSKEEPER I <div>Responsible for skilled maintenance of grass, plants, and trees, including determining and applying treatment to unhealthy plants.</div> Campus Facilities Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52437 2026-09-02T16:16:59-05:00 2026-09-02T16:16:59-05:00 TRANSIT SUPERVISOR (UTRGV EMPLOYEES ONLY) <div>To manage the day-to-day operations of campus shuttle services. Responsible to provide transportation services in a safe and timely manner.</div> Campus Auxiliary Services https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51669 2026-06-30T11:15:34-05:00 2026-06-30T11:15:35-05:00 ASSOCIATE RESEARCH SCIENTIST <div>Under limited supervision and with considerable latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment, performs advanced research work by coordinating the development, implementation, and monitoring of specialized research projects. Manages the upkeep, training, and supervision of specialized research equipment within area of assigned responsibility.</div> School of Medicine / MDOISU Cancer Research https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52283 2026-08-19T17:03:22-05:00 2026-08-19T17:03:23-05:00 ASSISTANT VICE PRESIDENT REVENUE CYCLE OPERATIONS <div>Responsible for providing operational leadership, strategic direction, and oversight of revenue cycle, credentialing, provider enrollment, payer relations, patient experience and patient access operations for UT Health RGV.</div> School of Medicine/ Revenue Cycle https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52209 2026-08-13T15:24:40-05:00 2026-08-13T15:24:40-05:00 Research Assistant_Informatics & Engineering Systems <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters. Maximum appointment may be increased up to forty (40) hours per week (100% FTE) during the summer if funded by a grant.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Informatics & Engineering Systems https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51847 2026-07-17T12:13:15-05:00 2026-07-17T12:13:15-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant / Marine Ecosystems Institute <div>Research Assistants will be assigned to assist a faculty member with data collection, analyzation, publication of data, and other duties as assigned.</div> Marine Ecosystems Institute https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52402 2026-08-31T16:14:00-05:00 2026-08-31T16:14:01-05:00 INSTITUTIONAL TITLE IX AND EQUAL OPPORTUNITY INVESTIGATOR / SENIOR INSTITUTIONAL TITLE IX AND EQUAL OPPORTUNITY INVESTIGATOR <div><strong>INSTITUTIONAL TITLE IX AND EQUAL OPPORTUNITY INVESTIGATOR:</strong><br>Supports the Chief Equal Opportunity &amp; Title IX Officer at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley by performing fact-gathering and investigative functions primarily related to discrimination, equal opportunity, sexual misconduct, and retaliation complaints by employees, students, and others protected under state or federal civil rights and anti-discrimination laws.<br><strong><br>SENIOR INSTITUTIONAL TITLE IX AND EQUAL OPPORTUNITY INVESTIGATOR:</strong><br>Supports the Chief Equal Opportunity &amp; Title IX Officer in the oversight of the Office of Title IX &amp; Equal Opportunity, at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley by performing highly specialized non-routine fact-gathering and investigative functions primarily related to complaints by employees, students, and others protected under state or federal civil rights and anti-discrimination laws, which involve allegations of discrimination, sexual misconduct, or retaliation.</div> Title IX & Equal Opportunity https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51156 2026-05-14T17:47:53-05:00 2026-05-14T17:47:54-05:00 One Year Appointment-Clinical Assistant Professor/School of Nursing <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a <strong>One Year Appointment- Clinical Assistant Professor</strong> of the <em>School of Nursing </em>beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. Duties may include teaching students in classrooms, simulated laboratories, and clinical settings as well as student advisement. Additional efforts in professional achievement and professional service are expected. UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to scholarly work, student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions and are committed to UTRGV’s strategic plan, vision, mission, values and core priorities (https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/).<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong><br><br></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div><div><br><strong>Department/College Background<br></strong>The School of Nursing offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in Nursing. These degrees include a traditional BSN and 2nd degree BSN pre-licensure degree, an RN to BSN, along with graduate degrees in Nursing Education, Nursing Administration, Family Nurse Practitioner, a Post-graduate certificate in Psychiatric Mental Health NP and our new Doctor in Nursing Practice (DNP) that started in Fall 2022. Our faculty teach on two campuses, in both Edinburg and in Brownsville. We have full simulation labs that offer state-of-the-art educational opportunities for all our students. We collaborate with the other health science programs at UTRGV on interdisciplinary clinical experiences and work with hospitals throughout the entire Rio Grande Valley. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution, UTRGV is committed to preparing its students to succeed, contribute and excel in an increasingly diverse, global, and interconnected world, and seeks faculty who are prepared to help in this goal.</div> School of Nursing https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50650 2026-03-30T15:17:46-05:00 2026-03-30T15:17:46-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Organization & School Leadership <div>The Department of Organization &amp; School Leadership at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) occasionally needs to hire non-tenure track, part-time lecturers to teach the at graduate level for the academic year 2026-2027.<br><br></div><div>Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction within the program.<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.<br><br></div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div><br>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit<a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/newsroom/2020/09/17-utrgv-marks-record-high-enrollment-student-success-outcomes-amid-pandemics-challenges.htm#:~:text=UTRGV%20announced%20Thursday%20that%20its,from%20the%20previous%20fall%20semester\"><strong>website</strong></a>.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Organization and School Leadership https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52120 2026-08-06T15:41:32-05:00 2026-08-06T15:41:32-05:00 Part-time Lecturer in Kinesiology & Exercise Science in HHP 2026-2027 <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a Part-Time Lecturer of <em>the Department of Health and Human Performance </em>beginning in the 2025-2026 academic year to teach in its Bachelor’s/Master’s Kinesiology, Exercise Science and Health programs. Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction within the program in the required format. UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to scholarly work, student success, and to advancing the university, college, and program missions and are committed to UTRGV’s strategic plan, vision, mission, values, and core priorities.(https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/)</div><div><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of University discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit our <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/about/index.htm\"><strong>website</strong></a>.</div><div><strong>Department/CollegeBackground</strong></div><div>The Department of Health and Human Performance is under the UTRGV College of Health Professions and offers BS degrees in Kinesiology, Health, and Exercise Science. It offers MS degrees in Kinesiology, Exercise Science and a certificate in Health Professions Education and Technology.</div> College of Health Professions / Health and Human Performance https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52441 2026-09-03T10:03:07-05:00 2026-09-03T10:03:07-05:00 Clinical Neurologist – Cognitive – Open Rank <div>The Department of Neuro and Behavioral Health at the University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) seeks a motivated and energetic candidate for an open rank position in the non-tenure academic clinician track, with expertise in managing and treating various cognitive specific disorders. These disorders may include but, not be limited to Alzheimer’s disease (or other forms of dementia), Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI), Vascular Cognitive Impairment, Frontotemporal dementia, Traumatic Brain injury, Stroke-related cognitive changes, Epilepsy, Neurodegenerative diseases, and brain tumors, The successful candidate should also be able to treat other general neurological disorders.<br><br></div><div>The ideal candidate will continue the growth and sustainability of the residency program to include but not be limited to teaching, further developing the Neurology residency (according to ACGME accreditation requirements) with GME leaders, ISU, leading didactics, sustaining and growing collaborative community partnerships in the Rio Grande Valley. Furthermore, the ideal candidate will provide outpatient care at UT Health’s Neurology Clinic located at the Institute of Neuroscience and potentially with other clinical partners with or without trainees.<br><br></div><div>Responsibilities will include teaching UTRGV School of Medicine students and residents (Neurology, Psychiatry, Internal Medicine, Family Medicine, and Podiatry).</div><div>The outpatient clinic is located at the Institute of Neuroscience in Harlingen, Texas.</div> School of Medicine / NBHISU Neuroscience https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51690 2026-06-30T15:03:00-05:00 2026-06-30T15:03:01-05:00 Graduate Assistant Physician Assistant 2026-2027 <div>To assist students, prepare for their exams.</div><div><br></div> College of Health Professions / Physician Assistant https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52311 2026-08-21T09:09:56-05:00 2026-08-21T09:09:57-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant - Clinical Psychology PhD <div>Maximum appointment is limited to ten (10) hours per week (25% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Psychological Science https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51210 2026-05-20T08:08:40-05:00 2026-05-20T08:08:40-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant - College of Education and P-16 Integration AY 26-27 <div>The College of Education and P-16 Integration is seeking to hire master’s and doctoral level students to be employed as Graduate Research Assistants throughout the 2026-2027 academic year. In the role of Graduate Research Assistant, the student will have the opportunity to support faculty with their research while gaining valuable mentorship from the faculty as they collaborate to produce publishable research projects or external research grant proposals. GRAs are assigned to specific research projects and will work directly with the faculty who are conducting those projects.<br><br>Graduate Research Assistants’ work time should be spent on research-related work. Duties will vary depending on the project and assigned research/scholarly functions or other creative projects. Examples of research-related work may include but are not limited to:<br><br></div><ul><li>Completion of Human Subjects Protection Training</li><li>Transcribing interview data</li><li>Locating professional articles on a research topic</li><li>Writing a literature review</li><li>Running statistical analyses</li><li>Organizing data into Excel and SPSS</li><li>Collecting data through interviews and/or surveys</li><li>Assisting in the preparation of conference presentation proposals</li><li>Creating PowerPoints or handouts for research presentations at conferences</li><li>Writing parts of a manuscript such as implications for practice</li><li>Editing and preparing a manuscript for submission to a peer-reviewed journal</li><li>Other research-related duties as assigned</li></ul><div><br><strong>Required Documents</strong></div><div>1.Curriculum Vitae or Resume</div><div>2.Writing Sample<br>3.Other - Recommendation Letter<br>4. Cover letter that addresses the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Why are you interested to become a Graduate Research Assistant (GRA) in the College of Education and P-16 Integration?</li><li>What are your research interests?</li><li>How much experience do you have working in Research? Please elaborate on the experience as well as roles/tasks you have served in the research process, if applicable.</li><li>How much experience do you have working with external research grant proposals or projects? Please elaborate on the roles/tasks you have served in the grant writing process, if applicable.</li><li>What is your academic background and what are your relevant work experiences that will help you work as a GRA in the College of Education and P-16 Integration (see <strong>scope of job above</strong> for information about possible research-related responsibilities)?</li><li>What are your long-term educational (e.g., Master’s degree, PhD, etc.) and career (e.g., position in higher education, K-12 administrator, etc.) goals?</li><li>What knowledge and skills do you hope to gain from your experience as a GRA in the College of Education and P-16 Integration?</li><li>What type of mentoring and feedback do you hope to receive from working as a GRA?</li><li>Are you fluent in multiple languages? Please specify the language(s) and level of fluency in speaking, reading, writing.</li></ul> College of Education and P-16 Integration https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52234 2026-08-17T10:01:32-05:00 2026-08-17T10:01:32-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant-Validation of the Spanish Grant <div>The Research Assistant will support a project focused on the <strong>Validation of the Spanish Grant</strong>, with responsibilities related to research recruitment, data collection, data analysis, and community outreach. The student will assist with implementing research activities, engaging with community members and participants, organizing and collecting project data, and supporting data analysis and interpretation.</div> School of Social Work https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51915 2026-07-22T10:28:37-05:00 2026-07-22T10:28:38-05:00 School of Music:  Part-Time Lecturer – Applied Music <div>The School of Music at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) occasionally needs to hire Music Part-Time Lecturers to teach in its Bachelor’s/Master’s program for the Fall 2026 &amp; Spring 2027. This position is contingent upon the enrollment and scheduling needs of the Music program. Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction in the program, advising students, and participating in scholarship activities serving the college, university, or local community as needed.<br><br></div><div>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions, as well as a commitment to UTRGV’s guiding principles (<a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/\"><strong>https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/</strong></a>), which include promoting access to postsecondary education to a diverse student body and to become one of the largest and most successful Hispanic-serving emerging research institutions in the U.S.A.<br><br></div><div>Teaching assignments include Applied Lessons in a variety of instruments and other courses as needed.&nbsp;</div> College of Fine Arts / Music https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52404 2026-09-01T08:39:20-05:00 2026-09-01T08:39:20-05:00 WS Graduate Assistant - Degree Progress & Graduation Initiatives <div><strong>Description of Duties:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide guidance and support to students seeking assistance from program.</li><li>May lead or support student success projects related to communication, outreach, data analysis, workshops, academic innovation, presentations, and social media.</li><li>Develop resources and guides geared at helping students prepare for graduation.</li><li>Work with student success and academic tools, technology platforms/applications, or CRM software.</li><li>Assist with complex student inquiries, solution finding, and making referrals to appropriate campus resources when needed.</li><li>Collaborate with campus partners, faculty, or students regarding assigned initiatives.</li><li>Tracking and progress monitoring of students for assigned initiative.</li><li>May perform research functions on topics relating to student success, academic support, university degree planning, student progress, and degree completion.</li><li>Review data to gather insights relating to student progress and degree completion.</li><li>Provide support to unit and assist with additional responsibilities as assigned.</li><li>This position will be in office</li></ul> Office of Student Success https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52325 2026-08-24T09:04:08-05:00 2026-08-24T09:04:08-05:00 Part Time Senior Lecturer Physical Therapy CoHP 2026-2027 <div>The Department of Physical Therapy at the University of Texas Rio Grande Valley is inviting applications for <strong>4 part-time faculty in the CAPTE Candidate Doctoral Physical Therapy Program</strong>. This is a solicitation for 4 part-time senior lecturers. Faculty rank and salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications and based on established university and department standards. The start date for the positions is 25 Aug 2026. The positions will require course development and instruction being provided in the summer, fall or spring academic semesters.&nbsp;</div><div>The successful candidate will develop and teach coursework in one or more of several physical therapy courses. Courses we are seeking support for include: foundational courses such as Physical Therapy Examination Techniques and Therapeutic Exercise, specialty courses such as Health and Wellness, Chronic Disorders, Management of Pelvic Floor Dysfunction, and Orthotics and Prosthetics. Additionally, faculty will mentor physical therapy students and participate in professional and community service.&nbsp;</div><div><br>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a senior lecturer beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;<br>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being.&nbsp; The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Department/College Background</strong></div><div><br>The College of Health Professions (CoHP) at UTRGV includes seven health professions departments with 11 undergraduates, twelve graduate and three doctoral degree programs. The CoHP and programmatic faculty work closely with the UTRGV School of Medicine, School of Podiatric Medicine, School of Nursing and the UT Health System to provide robust interprofessional education opportunities and training experiences for health professions students.&nbsp;</div><div>The Department of Physical Therapy is housed in a 55,000 sqft facility in Harlingen, Texas. The department is currently completing renovations for a state-of-the-art facility that will include three large classrooms, two large teaching laboratories, an anatomy suite with cadaveric and dry-lab teaching areas, three core research labs and ample office and student-centric learning spaces. Beginning in 2027, the building will be shared with the Department of Occupational Therapy who will have independent, state-of-the-art teaching, and research spaces. The DPT program is a nine-semester (three-year), full-time face-to-face program. The program serves a unique role in the PT profession in general and the Rio Grande Valley specifically to improve access to and quality of physical therapy services to rural and medically underserved areas in South Texas through education, research and community engagement and outreach.&nbsp;</div> College of Health Professions/Physical Therapy https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50789 2026-04-13T08:22:52-05:00 2026-04-13T08:22:52-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Registrar <div>Office of the Registrar is looking for Graduate students seeking a part-time position to provide support and assistance.<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists with processing of CSCR (Class Schedule Change Request) forms for different semester terms.&nbsp;</li><li>Reviews and approves event requests in Ad Astra for academic spaces.</li><li>Assists with special projects and tasks related to academic and event scheduling.</li><li>Reviews reports for academic class schedules for the different semester terms. &nbsp;</li><li>Provides specialized support that requires computer skills, data entry accuracy and software savviness.</li><li>Provides support to Scheduling Coordinator and team.&nbsp;</li><li>Performs other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Registrar https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52130 2026-08-07T12:53:46-05:00 2026-08-07T12:53:48-05:00 MEDICAL ASSISTANT <div>To provide excellent customer service as a first point of contact in an inter-professional clinic for the care of triply diagnosed (mental illness, chronic disease, and appetitive drive disorder) of an assigned population with excellent interpersonal, oral, written, and listening skills in Spanish and English.</div> School of Medicine / Ambulatory Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52446 2026-09-03T13:51:12-05:00 2026-09-03T13:51:12-05:00 BUILDING ATTENDANT I - NIGHT <div>To perform routine manual work involving the custodial maintenance of buildings.</div> Campus Facilities Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51693 2026-06-30T15:28:29-05:00 2026-06-30T15:28:29-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant Physical Therapy 2026-2027 <ol><li>collect data for research purposes</li><li>work with faculty to assist in data collection</li><li>keep a log of research activity</li><li>submit a summary of the research activity at the end of each semester.</li></ol><div><br></div> College of Health Professions/Physical Therapy https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51239 2026-05-22T16:54:48-05:00 2026-05-22T16:54:49-05:00 Part-Time Clinical Faculty (Supervisor) Communication Sciences & Disorders-CoHP 2026-2027 <div>The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) occasionally has the need to hire Part-Time Clinical Supervisors to Supervise in its Master of Communication Sciences and Disorders program. Responsibilities include delivering quality clinical instruction and supervision within the program. UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to scholarly work, student success and to advancing the university, college, and program missions and are committed to UTRGV’s strategic plan, vision, mission, values and core priorities. (https://www.utrgv.edu/strategic-plan/introduction/index.htm)</div> College of Health Professions  / Communication Disorders https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52238 2026-08-17T10:38:28-05:00 2026-08-17T10:38:28-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Communication <div>Will work as speech coach in the Hauser Lab assisting both undergraduate and graduate students with their speech performances. Promote the Hauser Lab through classroom visits and workshops Maximum appointment is limited to 50% FTE (20 hours per week) May need to travel to the Brownsville Campus once a week.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Communication https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/49160 2025-10-28T10:45:44-05:00 2025-10-28T10:45:45-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant for Health Sciences 2025-2026 <div>Dr. Batholomew Chireh at the Department of Health Sciences, University of Texas Rio Grande Valley, on the Edinburg Campus, invites applications for a part-time contract Graduate Research Assistant position. The successful applicant will be involved in various research projects, but I will expect most of his/her work will be dedicated towards a pilot study assessing ergonomic risk factors and heat exposure as determinants of musculoskeletal disorders and mental wellbeing among port personnel in the Rio Grande Valley.</div> College of Health Professions/Health Sciences https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51949 2026-07-24T10:38:28-05:00 2026-07-24T10:38:29-05:00 Assistant Professor (Exercise Science) Health & Human Performance CoHP Tenure-Track Faculty 2027-2028 <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as an <em>Assistant Professor </em>of <em>Health &amp; Human Performance </em>beginning in the <strong>2027-2028</strong> academic year.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div><br>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div><div><strong>Department/College Background</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The Department of Health &amp; Human Performance in the College of Health Professions is seeking qualified candidates who have demonstrated a record of success in research, teaching, and professional service in exercise science or kinesiology as Assistant Professor to begin Fall 2027. The position is a nine-month tenure-track faculty position. The responsibilities include establishing and maintaining a focused research agenda, procurement of external grants, participation in scholarly committees and taskforces, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in exercise science or kinesiology, and performing other duties assigned by the department chair. Given that UTRGV is a distributed campus faculty will be required to teach in a variety of settings, incorporating technology and student-engaged pedagogies to maximize student success, and may be assigned to teach face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online courses. Service to the department, college, university, community, and professional organizations is an integral part of the faculty member’s responsibilities.</div><div><br>UTRGV faculty will be expected to demonstrate a strong commitment to student success and to advancing the university, college and program mission and be committed to UTRGV’s guiding principles (<a href=\"http://utrgv.edu/en-us/about-utrgv/history/transition-plan/guiding-principles/\"><strong>http://utrgv.edu/en-us/about-utrgv/history/transition-plan/guiding-principles/</strong></a>), which include promoting access to postsecondary education to a diverse student body and to become one of the largest and most successful Hispanic-serving emerging research institutions in the U.S.A.</div><div><br>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as an Assistant Professor of Exercise Science in the College of Health Professions beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year.</div><div><br>College Information</div><div><br>The College of Health Professions is the leading institution of excellence in health and human services, education, health care and research. Our main goal is to produce highly skilled practitioners, educators, and researchers through our high quality educational programs. Students who are accepted into our programs enter into an educational environment, which through student centered, meaningful experiential learning opportunities, results in the development of new scientific and intellectual inquiry for the promotion of health equity in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond.</div><div><br>The College houses one school, nine departments, the Border Health Office and other health centers and organizations that are focused on improving the health of our South Texas Community. In the College of Health Professions at UTRGV, we are dedicated to training the next generation of health professionals and leaders to fill the roles of practitioner, educator and researcher in the 21st Century.</div><div><br>Our Vision</div><div><br>We envision the College of Health Professions as a world-class institution committed to achieving the highest quality of life and health equity through education, research, and engagement with our communities.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Our Mission</div><div><br>The College of Health Professions will be the leading institution of excellence in health and human services, education, health care and research, producing highly skilled practitioners, educators, and researchers through high quality educational programs, meaningful experiential learning opportunities and the development of scientific and intellectual inquiry for the promotion of health equity in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond.</div> College of Health Professions / Health and Human Performance https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52412 2026-09-01T10:10:05-05:00 2026-09-01T10:10:06-05:00 FINANCIAL MANAGER <div>To manage the daily operations and functions of an assigned finance or accounting unit. Responsible for supervising staff assigned to the area and implementing strategic programs to ensure the improvement of the department’s business processes in accordance with the University’s mission and goals.</div> Office of Research https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51726 2026-07-06T11:29:01-05:00 2026-07-06T11:29:02-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Counseling <div>The Department of Counseling at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) may have the need to hire non-tenure track, part-time Lecturers to teach in the Master of Education in Counseling program for the academic year 2026-2027. Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction within the program.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.<br><br></div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.<br><br></div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit our <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/about/index.htm\"><strong>website</strong></a>.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Counseling https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52340 2026-08-25T10:04:53-05:00 2026-08-25T10:04:54-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant - MDOISU McAllen <ul><li>Searching for and reviewing published literature on a research topic.</li><li>Helping to develop a project methodology.</li><li>Assisting with lab work.</li><li>Taking notes.</li><li>Attending team or project meetings.</li><li>Assisting in developing resources for project management.</li><li>Collecting data.</li></ul><div><br></div> School of Medicine / Medicine and Oncology ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50802 2026-04-13T16:08:36-05:00 2026-04-13T16:08:36-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer - Student Teaching Supervisor <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as a Part-Time Lecturer – Student Teaching Supervisor of</div><div>Teaching and Learning in the 2025-2026 academic year.</div><div><br>The Department of Teaching &amp; Learning at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) occasionally has the need to hire Part-Time Lecturers to supervise, during the school day, teachers for undergraduate teacher preparation programs starting Fall 2025 through Spring 2026 Semester.<br><br>• delivering quality instruction within the respective programs;<br>• providing guidance and support of the clinical teacher and cooperating teacher during school hours (8:00am-4:00pm) ;observing, assessing, and evaluating clinical teachers during school hours;<br>• communicating and providing feedback to clinical teacher and cooperating teacher;<br>• participating in all clinical teaching program assessments; and<br>• completing and collecting all required documentation.<br>• Support cooperating teacher in completion of required performance evaluations, time log approvals, candidate dispositions, etc<br>• Maintain open and continuous communication with the Office of Field Experiences<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of University discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) iscommitted to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do,including teaching, research, and service.</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit our <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/about/index.htm\"><strong>website</strong></a>.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Teaching and Learning https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52132 2026-08-07T12:55:11-05:00 2026-08-07T12:55:13-05:00 PATIENT SERVICES REPRESENTATIVE I <div>Responsible for greeting and registering patients in a caring and warm manner, handle in-coming patient telephone calls, scheduling appointments, handling patient queries, collecting and obtaining accurate insurance information, and time of service collections as required.</div> School of Medicine / Ambulatory Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52449 2026-09-03T14:39:33-05:00 2026-09-03T14:39:34-05:00 IT MEDIA SYSTEMS TECHNICIAN I <div>To provide the daily operation, installation, troubleshooting, and maintenance of all assigned IT Media Systems, such as classroom technology systems, videoconferencing technology systems, and digital signage technology systems in support of UTRGV faculty, students, staff and visitors.</div> Infrastructure & Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51362 2026-06-05T13:15:12-05:00 2026-06-05T13:15:12-05:00 Primary Care Sports Medicine / Non-operative Sports Medicine Orthopedic Physician <div>UTRGV School of Medicine Department of Orthopedics seeks a Primary Care Sports Medicine Physician/Non-operative Sports Medicine Physician. Candidates should be board certified/board eligible and have completed an accredited Sports Medicine Fellowship. Responsibilities will include patient care, teaching residents and medical students, collegiate and high school athletics coverage, and opportunities for clinical research.<br><br></div> School of Medicine / Surgical Specialty and MSK ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52242 2026-08-17T13:24:42-05:00 2026-08-17T13:24:43-05:00 RESEARCH ASSOCIATE II <div>Under the general supervision and with moderate latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment, performs moderately complex specialized research projects. May supervise the work of others.</div> College of Sciences/ Ctr VectrBrne Zoontc Emgng Dis https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/49551 2025-12-01T14:05:25-06:00 2025-12-01T14:05:26-06:00 Director of the School of Rehabilitation Services and Counseling <div>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) invites nominations and applications for the position of Director of the School of Rehabilitation Services &amp; Counseling. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Health Professions, within the Division of Health Affairs, the director provides strategic leadership, fosters academic excellence, and ensures alignment with the goals of the College of Health Professions and the broader university. This position is equivalent to a department chair and plays a critical role in advancing the school’s mission in teaching, research, service, and community engagement. The college seeks a dynamic leader who will collaborate with faculty, staff, and students to foster a culture of excellence.<br><br>UTRGV was created by the Texas Legislature in 2013 as the first major public university of the 21st century in Texas and is the second-largest Hispanic-serving institution in the United States. The majority of its students are bilingual and bicultural. UTRGV is located in a growing, vibrant region on the border with Mexico, which boasts many diverse cultural, ecological, and recreational activities.<br><br>UTRGV is establishing a Division of Health Affairs to help grow UT Health RGV and ensure the participation of all health-related programs and create a stronger framework for collaboration and impact among health-related programs. The goal is for the division to boost interdisciplinary learning, enhance patient care, and support UT Health RGV’s growing clinical services, including the upcoming Cancer &amp; Surgery Center and Diabetes Center of Excellence. The Division of Health Affairs aligns the Schools of Medicine, Podiatric Medicine, Nursing, Optometry (launching in 2027, pending accreditation), and the College of Health Professions.<br><br>The School of Rehabilitation Services &amp; Counseling is a dynamic academic unit dedicated to preparing professionals to assist people with disabilities to live full and independent lives. The School of Rehabilitation Services &amp; Counseling currently has 18 full-time (tenured, tenure track, and non-tenured) faculty teaching in the program and over 350 students enrolled. Located in a modern facility (Edinburg Health Affairs Building West) featuring dedicated classrooms and a state-of-the-art Counseling &amp; Wellness Center and Research Center, the school prides itself on preparing students to enter a rewarding field of helping others to achieve their own goals of independence and productivity.<br><br><strong>Leadership Role of the Director</strong><br><br>The Director of the School of Rehabilitation Services &amp; Counseling serves as the academic and administrative leader of the school, equivalent to a department chair, at UTRGV. This role requires visionary leadership, strategic planning, and a commitment to advancing the mission of the university and the College of Health Professions.<br><br>The Director is expected to:</div><ul><li>Provide strategic academic leadership to advance the school’s mission in teaching, research, and service, with a focus on innovation, excellence, and impact.</li><li>Drive enrollment growth at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, with a particular emphasis on expanding and strengthening the PhD program.</li><li>Champion research development, fostering a culture of inquiry and scholarship that supports UTRGV’s goal of achieving R1 status as designated by the Carnegie Commission.</li><li>Cultivate a collaborative and inclusive academic community, promoting shared governance, transparency, and mutual respect among faculty, staff, and students.</li><li>Lead the school’s administrative operations, including budget management, policy enforcement, and resource allocation to support strategic priorities.</li><li>Recruit, retain, and mentor high-quality faculty and staff, supporting their professional development and fostering a culture of academic excellence.</li><li>Oversee faculty evaluation, promotion, and development processes, ensuring alignment with university standards and best practices in higher education.</li><li>Strengthen external partnerships and interdisciplinary collaborations, enhancing the school’s visibility and impact within the university and broader community.</li><li>Advance curricular innovation and student success initiatives, ensuring academic programs are responsive to evolving professional and societal needs.</li><li>Foster effective communication and conflict resolution, addressing concerns and promoting a positive and productive academic climate.</li><li>Engage stakeholders in shaping the school’s direction, including faculty, students, alumni, community partners, and university leadership.</li></ul><div><br>As a faculty member, the Director is also expected to maintain an active role in teaching (with a reduced load), research, and service, modeling the values of academic engagement and leadership.</div> College of Health Professions  / Rehabilitation Services and Counseling https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51990 2026-07-28T15:06:16-05:00 2026-07-28T15:06:16-05:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant - Computer Science <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE).</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Computer Science https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52415 2026-09-01T10:15:17-05:00 2026-09-01T10:15:18-05:00 SCHOOL OF MEDICINE- UNDERGRADUATE MEDICAL EDUCATION CURRICULUM MANAGER <div>To manage and maintain the educational quality of the Undergraduate Medical Education (UME) program and ensure compliance with the Licensing Committee on Medical Education (LCME) accreditation standards, SOM Central Curriculum Authority Committee (CCAC) guidelines and other regulatory requirements. Responsible for the alignment, implementation and compliance of the LCME standards and managing real-time curricular and assessment mapping.</div> Ofc of Educational Affairs https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51762 2026-07-09T11:14:15-05:00 2026-07-09T11:14:16-05:00 Medical Assistant (UT Health RGV Orthopedics and Sports Medicine) <div>To provide excellent customer service and clinical care for patients of the UTRGV School of Medicine / UT Health Rio Grande Valley using interpersonal skills for oral, written and listening skills in Spanish and English.</div> School of Medicine / Surgical Specialty and MSK ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52360 2026-08-25T17:38:30-05:00 2026-08-25T17:38:31-05:00 UNIVERSITY POLICE OFFICER I <div>To enforce the law, provide service, information and aid to all citizens as circumstances require, prevent crime, suppress disturbances, investigate criminal offenses, and arrest offenders. Serves as a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act).<br><br>Responsible for enforcement duties for the protection, safety and welfare of students, employees, visitors, and all property within the area under the control and jurisdiction of The University of Texas System. Exercises independent judgment within the limits prescribed by law, Rules and Regulations of the Board of Regents, institutional rules and regulations and Director of Police departmental policies and procedures.</div> University Police https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50826 2026-04-15T10:16:19-05:00 2026-04-15T10:16:19-05:00 Academic Psychiatrist <div><br>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley School of Medicine Department of Psychiatry seeks a Psychiatrist for inpatient and outpatient services. In addition, they will participate in scholarly activity, faculty development, patient safety and quality improvement initiatives, prepare and provide didactics, and participate in the evaluation of the residents and medical students. While previous experience in a residency program teaching role is preferred, individuals just finishing residency/fellowship training are highly encouraged to apply. Faculty are expected to administer and maintain a professional educational environment conducive to educating residents in each of the ACGME competencies, assisting them to reach their individual Milestones, plus educating medical students in the practice of Psychiatry. Working within the UT Health RGV clinical mission, the Department has outstanding educational and scholarly activities for medical students and a growing Psychiatry program. Demonstration of strong commitment to the education of residents and medical students is essential. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishments and experience.</div> School of Medicine / NBHISU Psych Neuro & Optometry https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52146 2026-08-10T12:45:04-05:00 2026-08-10T12:45:04-05:00 PhD MSE - Research Assistant <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Mechanical Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52452 2026-