social media communication and campaigns related to the project/programs.</div><div>•May plan, develop, organize, and coordinate research and survey designs. Which can include data collection, processing, and analysis and evaluation of data. Dissemination of findings through publication of YouTube videos.</div><div>•May assists others in writing and developing proposals for funding grants.<br>•Attends meetings, conferences, and seminars related to the project's/program’s mission and goals.<br>•Helps supervise and organize seminars, conferences, and presentations.</div><div>•Provides appropriate reports as required for the projects/programs to Project Manager.</div><div>•May provide support in the coordination of general community and school gardens and related small-scale farm plots and farm site demonstration sites in an agricultural environment.</div><div><br></div> College of Sciences/ Sustainble Agr & Rural Advncmt https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/49955 2026-01-14T15:29:14-06:00 2026-01-14T15:29:14-06:00 Puentes Graduate Research Student Assistant <div>&nbsp;|<br>Student will engage in exclusive networking ,research, and professional development activities, participate in cohort-building events, and enjoy flexible work schedules that accommodate academic commitments. Puentes provides opportunities to learn beyond the classroom, develop critical skills like time management and communication, and gain confidence in a professional setting.<br>&nbsp;<br>Develop and maintain relationships with the community, university students, university faculty and staff who are a part of the Puentes year 2 workshops and help guide them on any questions they may have regarding the grant and their assignments.<br>&nbsp;Responsible for assisting with seminars, conferences, workshops, campus talks and events under the Puentes grant. Student will learn about Mexican American studies and social justice in our local school, University, and community and will work closely faculty and staff from various departments on helping develop their syllabi’s and SWOT (strengths, weakness, opportunities, threats) assignments to help create a sense of belonging in their classrooms and depts/centers.<br>&nbsp;Assist in the management- Students will manage their time as well as assist PI's on research for the grants assigned.<br>Graphic design, students will learn graphic design skills such as creating flyers, promotional items, website design and upkeep as well as how to use Adobe and other UTRGV media tools to maintain the grant.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Literatures and Cultural Studies https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52008 2026-07-29T14:23:48-05:00 2026-07-29T14:23:48-05:00 Research Assistant in Civil Engineering <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE) during the Fall and Spring semesters. Maximum appointment may be increased up to forty (40) hours per week (100% FTE) during the summer if funded by a grant.</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Civil Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51788 2026-07-13T13:32:03-05:00 2026-07-13T13:32:04-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Undergraduate Admissions <ul><li>Follows established policies, guidelines, and regulations to determine the appropriate department and course level for the incoming credits.</li><li>Serves as a resource for departmental advisors, students, faculty, and staff to interpret and explain policies, regulations, and guidelines related to transfer credit.</li><li>Creates and maintains the transfer articulation component in the student system.</li><li>Troubleshoots and implements the resolution of an individual student's problems which may arise during the transfer credit evaluation process.</li><li>Supports the processing of student applications and documents.</li><li>Performs other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Undergraduate Admissions https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52372 2026-08-27T09:19:21-05:00 2026-08-27T09:19:22-05:00 ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT OF HUMAN RESOURCES FOR HEALTH AFFAIRS <div>Oversees all facets of Human Resources for the Division of Health Affairs (DOHA) by leading independently various HR-related matters for both Executive, Faculty, Physician and Staff, including recruitment, performance management, HR policies, employee relations, progressive discipline, training, strategic planning, and organizational development.</div> Ofc of Health Affairs https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50850 2026-04-17T10:58:05-05:00 2026-04-17T10:58:05-05:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant - Manufacturing & Industrial Engineering <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE).</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Manufacturing and Industrial Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52166 2026-08-12T09:43:21-05:00 2026-08-12T09:43:22-05:00 ELECTRICIAN I <div>To provide journeyman level installation, maintenance, and service of electrical/electronic systems skills. Responsible for the prompt performance of assigned electrical/electronic and related duties.</div> Campus Facilities Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52459 2026-09-04T12:03:02-05:00 2026-09-04T12:03:02-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer Health & Biomedical Sciences (Master of Science in Health Sciences) 2026-2027 <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>student body as a <em>part-time lecturer in the Department of Health and Biomedical Sciences </em>beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond through an innovative, unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being.&nbsp; The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advances in research and creative work, expanding access to high-quality, affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of UTRGV students identify as Hispanic, making it one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> College of Health Professions  / Health and Biomedical Sciences https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52081 2026-08-04T11:02:06-05:00 2026-08-04T11:02:08-05:00 RECRUITER, HEALTH AFFAIRS <div>The recruiter will contribute to the planning and execution of various departmental faculty and staff recruitment related initiatives and partner with the Recruitment Manager to create and execute strategic recruitment plans in accordance with the needs and goals of the UTRGV Division of Health Affairs and UT Health RGV.</div> Ofc of Health Affairs https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52429 2026-09-02T10:33:21-05:00 2026-09-02T10:33:22-05:00 SENIOR ADMINISTRATIVE ASSOCIATE <div>To provide advanced and complex administrative support to a Vice President or similar level position and assumes considerable responsibility for office management. Responsible for many complex office decisions and administrative support, with minimal direction.</div> Ofc of Health Affairs https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51534 2026-06-18T11:13:25-05:00 2026-06-18T11:13:25-05:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant - Spanish Department <div>Perform responsibilities as determined by assigned faculty member(s) for teaching purposes.</div> College of Liberal Arts/Spanish https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52258 2026-08-18T14:05:56-05:00 2026-08-18T14:05:57-05:00 PRIOR AUTHORIZATION AND REFERRAL SPECIALIST <div>Responsible for obtaining and processing all prior authorizations and referrals and entering the completed referral into the electronic medical record system for claims adjudication to ensure services are validated.</div> School of Medicine/ Revenue Cycle https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50043 2026-01-23T16:33:21-06:00 2026-01-23T16:33:21-06:00 Graduate Assistant - Graduate Recruitment <div><strong>JOB DESCRIPTION</strong><br><br> We are seeking a highly motivated and enthusiastic Graduate Assistant to join our team and assist with our graduate recruitment efforts. As a Graduate Assistant, you will play a crucial role in attracting and advising prospective students about our graduate programs. Your primary responsibility will be to provide excellent customer service by answering inquiries and guiding prospective students through the admission process, requirements, and career outlook with a graduate degree. You will interact with prospective students via phone, email, text message, live chat, and video.<br><br></div><div><strong>DUTIES<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Provide exceptional customer service to prospective graduate students by promptly responding to inquiries via phone, email, text message, live chat, and video.</li><li>Assist prospective students with questions regarding the admission process, requirements, deadlines, program details, and career opportunities associated with our graduate programs.</li><li>Maintain a thorough knowledge and understanding of all graduate programs offered, including program prerequisites, curriculum, faculty, and any program-specific requirements.</li><li>Effectively communicate the benefits and advantages of pursuing a graduate degree at UTRGV, highlighting unique features and opportunities.</li><li>Coordinate and schedule appointments and information sessions for prospective students, ensuring a seamless and positive experience.</li><li>Collaborate with the Graduate Recruitment team to organize and participate in recruitment events, such as graduate fairs, information sessions, and webinars.</li><li>Assist in the development and enhancement of recruitment materials, including brochures, presentations, and website content.</li><li>Maintain accurate records of prospective student interactions and inquiries using the appropriate customer relationship management (CRM) tools.</li><li>Assist with other graduate recruitment duties as assigned, which may include data entry, administrative tasks, or support during recruitment campaigns.</li></ul> Graduate Recruitment https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52464 2026-09-04T17:17:46-05:00 2026-09-04T17:17:47-05:00 PUBLIC SAFETY OFFICER <div>To provide service and information to students, employees and visitors; to enforce the rules and regulations of the U.T. System Administration or an institution of The University of Texas System pertaining to the operation and parking of vehicles on University property; to help safeguard property of the U.T. System Administration or an institution of The University of Texas System. Responsible for enforcing the regulations pertaining to the parking of vehicles on University controlled property; directing traffic; patrolling University controlled property for the purpose of safeguarding buildings and property under the control and jurisdiction of the U.T. System Administration or an institution of The University of Texas System.</div> University Police https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51810 2026-07-14T13:39:06-05:00 2026-07-14T13:39:06-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Digital Marketing Assistant FY27 <div>Seeking an innovative and proactive Graduate Assistant to enhance our digital marketing and advertising efforts across multiple platforms. In this role, you will focus on creating and managing video content as well as supporting broader digital marketing campaigns. This includes executing and optimizing digital advertising campaigns on platforms such as Meta Ads, developing targeted content strategies, and driving engagement through effective audience interaction. The ideal candidate is passionate about digital marketing, adept in video storytelling, and eager to leverage the latest technologies and trends to achieve outstanding marketing results.<br><br></div><div><strong>Digital Marketing Campaigns</strong>: Assist in the planning and execution of digital marketing campaigns that leverage video content to drive engagement and meet strategic objectives. Participate in brainstorming sessions and contribute creative ideas.<br><br></div><div><strong>Digital Advertising Support:</strong> Assist in managing and optimizing digital advertising campaigns on Meta Ads. This includes updating ad copy, refining audience targeting, and enhancing creative elements to improve campaign performance and ROI.<br><br></div><div><strong>Video Content Creation:</strong> Develop and produce engaging video content tailored for various social media platforms, including but not limited to Instagram, Facebook, and YouTube. This includes conceptualizing ideas, filming, and post-production editing.<br><br></div><div><strong>Social Media Support:</strong> Collaborate with the digital marketing team to schedule and optimize the distribution of video content across social media channels. Monitor engagement and analytics to gauge content performance and suggest improvements.<br><br></div><div><strong>Research and Trends:</strong> Stay up-to-date with the latest trends in video content and social media marketing to propose innovative ideas that can elevate our brand's digital presence.</div> University Marketing and Communications https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52392 2026-08-31T10:51:36-05:00 2026-08-31T10:51:36-05:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant Fall 2026 - RCV College of Business Dean's Office <div>Location: Campus in either Edinburg, Texas and/or Brownsville, Texas.<br><br>Duties include, but are not limited to, providing feedback and/or grading student work; monitoring/proctoring course activities; leading laboratory sessions, discussion sessions, or recitation labs; providing office hour assistance to students; and performing clerical tasks associated with course instruction.</div> RCV College of Business and Entrepreneurship https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51064 2026-05-06T09:37:53-05:00 2026-05-06T09:37:53-05:00 Graduate Assistant- Mexican American Studies <div>Assist faculty with administrative work, office hours and other duties as needed. Maximum appointment is limited to 25% FTE (10 hours per week).</div> College of Liberal Arts / Literatures and Cultural Studies https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52189 2026-08-13T09:30:40-05:00 2026-08-13T09:30:41-05:00 POSTDOCTORAL FELLOW <div>Postdoctoral Fellow will work on a two-year research project funded through the USDA-APHIS New World Screwworm (NWS) Grand Challenge grant investigating the chemical ecology of NWS. The project focuses on the ecology of NWS. Its primary goal is to determine how plant- and animal-derived volatile compounds influence screwworm fly behavior, ecology, and reproduction. The project will also include development of integrated vegetation-based habitat suitability and dispersal models for screwworm in South Texas. This will be achieved by combining high-resolution remote sensing data with ecological and landscape variables to identify areas of potential establishment and inform management or sterile insect release strategies. Under minimal supervision, the Fellow will collaborate with the Principal Investigators (PIs) to design and implement laboratory and field-based research experiments. The Fellow is also expected to mentor graduate and undergraduate students; assist with data analysis; and contribute to the preparation of reports, manuscripts, and dissemination of research findings.</div> College of Sciences/ Ctr VectrBrne Zoontc Emgng Dis https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50147 2026-02-03T15:58:45-06:00 2026-02-03T15:58:45-06:00 Graduate Assistant -Int'l Bus & Entrepreneurship <div>The candidate will work with faculty to assist in events and recruitment efforts, supporting the department digital communication needs. The role may also include data entry, administrative tasks, support during recruitment campaigns and projects, and general office tasks such as clerical, posting announcements, uploading documents, etc.<br><br></div><div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE); assistantships are semester-based and subject to renewal each term.<br><br></div> RCV College of Business and Entrepreneurship / International Business and Entrepreneurship https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52101 2026-08-05T14:01:02-05:00 2026-08-05T14:01:03-05:00 MEDICAL REFERRAL COORDINATOR <div>Responsible for managing and coordinating incoming and outgoing patient referrals within UT Health RGV and to external community healthcare facilities and providers. To facilitate the seamless transfer of UT Health RGV patients to specialists within and outside of our healthcare providers, ensuring timely access to necessary medical services.</div> School of Medicine/ Revenue Cycle https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52432 2026-09-02T12:28:08-05:00 2026-09-02T12:28:08-05:00 OFFICE ASSISTANT <div>To perform clerical duties for a department. Responsible for the performance of clerical, typing and data entry duties.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Bilingual and Literacy Studies https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51580 2026-06-25T09:42:18-05:00 2026-06-25T09:42:18-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Teaching and Learning <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as a Part-Time Lecturer of Teaching and Learning in the <strong>2026-2027</strong>&nbsp;academic year.</div><div><br>The Department of Teaching &amp; Learning at The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) occasionally has the need to hire non-tenure track, part-time Lecturers to teach in its Bachelor’s program for the academic year 2023-2024, beginning with the Fall 2024 through Summer 2024 Semester. Responsibilities include delivering quality instruction within the program.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of University discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.<br><br></div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.<br><br></div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit our <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/about/index.htm\"><strong>website</strong></a>.</div> College of Education and P-16 Integration / Teaching and Learning https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52271 2026-08-19T09:53:06-05:00 2026-08-19T09:53:07-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Philosophy <div>The Graduate Assistant will provide programmatic, and research support to the Department of Philosophy's Master of Science in Bioethics program. Responsibilities may include assisting with student recruitment and outreach activities, maintaining program records, supporting online and in-person events, conducting literature reviews and research related to bioethics topics, assisting with grant-related activities, preparing reports and program materials, and supporting faculty initiatives associated with the MS in Bioethics program. The Graduate Assistant will work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students while contributing to the growth, promotion, and daily operations of the Bioethics program.</div> College of Liberal Arts / Philosophy https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51820 2026-07-15T11:10:30-05:00 2026-07-15T11:10:30-05:00 Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs, School of Medicine (UTRGV Employees Only) <div>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) School of Medicine invites applications for the position of <strong>Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs</strong>. This leader will set the strategic vision for faculty affairs, guide all faculty-related matters, and oversee operational functions of the Office of Faculty Affairs. This position reports directly to the Dean of the School of Medicine and collaborates with the faculty affairs unit within Division of Health Affairs.&nbsp;</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>Position Overview</strong>&nbsp;</div><div>The Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs provides strategic leadership and oversight of all faculty-related matters at The UTRGV School of Medicine. Independently and in collaboration with other leaders within the school and the division of health affairs, the Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs role includes engagement with and/or oversight of faculty appointments, faculty recruitment and retention, career development, including promotion and tenure processes, faculty-related personnel matters, including annual performance evaluations, professional development programs, well-being efforts, and governance issues and policies.&nbsp;</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong>&nbsp;</div><div>The Assistant Dean is responsible for providing visionary leadership and ensuring excellence in carrying out the responsibilities of the Office of Faculty Affairs, including:&nbsp;</div><ul><li><strong>Leadership:</strong> Serves on the dean’s executive leadership team and collaborates with chairs, other decanal leaders, senior administrators, professional staff, division of health affairs and institutional leaders, and practice plan partners to advance the mission of the school of medicine.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Faculty Development:</strong> Recruitment (in coordination with faculty recruitment), mentorship, evaluation, and promotion of regular and community faculty; fostering a culture of wellness, collaboration, and professional growth.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Administration:</strong> Financial oversight, budget planning, and resource allocation aligned with school, division and institutional priorities.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Strategic Planning:</strong> Development and implementation of departmental or division of health affairs strategies consistent with the School of Medicine’s mission.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Accreditation:</strong>&nbsp; Work closely with the assistant dean for accreditation to serve as a resource and in leading efforts among faculty to prepare for the continued successful accreditation of the school of medicine.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Representation:</strong> Serve as a representative for the school of medicine within the division of health affairs, the institution and at local, regional, state, and national levels.&nbsp;</li></ul><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>Additional Responsibilities (UTRGV School of Medicine Standard Expectations for faculty affairs)</strong>&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Work closely with chairs to support the management of their faculty, including orienting new faculty.&nbsp;</li><li>Monitor faculty teaching performance using appropriate systems and work with chairs to enhance performance and develop teaching improvement initiatives such as the teaching med ed certificate program&nbsp;</li><li>Work with the Committee on Committees and Faculty Advisory Committee to solicit faculty presentation on key committees.&nbsp;</li><li>Solicit applications for teaching, research, and other awards.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintain and updated faculty roster and faculty handbook. &nbsp;</li><li>Attend administrative meetings.&nbsp;</li></ul><div><br></div> Faculty Affairs SOM https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52397 2026-08-31T13:50:30-05:00 2026-08-31T13:50:30-05:00 Open Rank Assistant/Associate/Professor Rehabilitation Services & Counseling CoHP Tenure-Track Faculty 2027-2028 <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s student body as an <strong><em>Assistant/Associate/Professor</em></strong> of the School of Rehabilitation Services &amp; Counseling beginning in the <strong>2027-2028</strong> academic year.<br><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong><br><br>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.<br><br>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building on strengths in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.<br><br>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit UTRGV website.<br><br>Department/College Background<br><br><strong>The College</strong><br><br>The College of Health Professions will be the leading institute of excellence in health and human services, education, healthcare, and research, producing highly skilled practitioners, educators, and researchers through high-quality educational programs, meaningful experimental learning opportunities, and the development of scientific and intellectual inquiry for the promotion of health equity in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond.<br><br><strong>Academic Departments</strong><br><br>Department of Health &amp; Biomedical Sciences<br>Department of Communication Sciences &amp; Disorders<br>Department of Health &amp; Human Performance<br>Department of Occupational Therapy<br>Department of Physician Assistant Studies<br>Department of Physical Therapy<br>Department of Health Sciences<br>Department of Medical Laboratory Sciences<br>Department of Nutrition &amp; Dietetics<br>School of Rehabilitation Services and Counseling<br><br><strong>The School<br></strong><br>A dynamic academic unit dedicated to preparing professionals to assist people with disabilities in living full lives, the School of Rehabilitation Services &amp; Counseling currently has 16 full-time faculty members (tenured, tenure-track, and non-tenured) teaching in the program, and over 400 students are enrolled. Located in a modern facility (Edinburg Health Affairs Building West) featuring dedicated classrooms and a state-of-the-art research lab and counseling center, the school prides itself on preparing students to enter a rewarding field of helping others to achieve their own goals of independence and productivity.<br><br><strong>Accreditation</strong><br><br>The B.S. in Rehabilitation Services is accredited from November 2021 to December 2028 by the Committee on Rehabilitation Accreditation (CoRA) under the auspices of the Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs (CAAHEP).<br>The B.S. in Addiction Studies is accredited June 2023-December 2029 by the National Addiction Studies Accreditation Commission (NASAC).<br>The M.S. in Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling is accredited from July 2018 to October 2027 by the Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs (CACREP).<br>The Ph.D. in Rehabilitation Counseling (Counselor Education and Supervision) is accredited from January 2016 to October 2027 by the Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs<br>(CACREP).<br><br><strong>Degrees and Specializations</strong><br><br>Doctor of Philosophy in Rehabilitation Counseling<br>Master of Science in Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling<br>Bachelor of Science in Rehabilitation Services<br>Bachelor of Science in Addiction Studies<br>Certificate in Expressive Arts Therapy<br>Certificate in Bilingual Counseling<br><br><strong>Minors</strong><br><br>Rehabilitation Services<br>Addiction Studies<br>Expressive Arts Minor</div> College of Health Professions  / Rehabilitation Services and Counseling https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51081 2026-05-07T09:08:14-05:00 2026-05-07T09:08:15-05:00 Graduate Assistant- Literatures & Cultural Studies <div>Assist faculty with administrative work and with office duties as needed. Maximum appointment is limited to 50% FTE (20 hours per week).</div> College of Liberal Arts / Literatures and Cultural Studies https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52191 2026-08-13T09:42:38-05:00 2026-08-13T09:42:38-05:00 RESEARCH ASSOCIATE I <div>Under the moderate supervision and with limited latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment, performs routine research projects. May supervise the work of others.</div> College of Sciences/ Ctr VectrBrne Zoontc Emgng Dis https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50198 2026-02-09T14:30:01-06:00 2026-02-09T14:30:02-06:00 Part Time Lecturer in the Robert C. Vackar College of Business and Entrepreneurship/Marketing <div>We seek applicants who are dedicated to serving <strong>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley’s </strong>diverse student body as a Part Time Lecturer of <em>Department of Marketing Fall 2026.</em></div><div><br><strong>About UTRGV:</strong></div><div>UTRGV serves the Rio Grande Valley and beyond via an innovative and unique multicultural education dedicated to student access and success. By championing leading research, healthcare, and application of university discoveries, we support sustainable development, community engagement, and well-being. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) is committed to building and sustaining a highly qualified and talented faculty to pursue excellence in everything that we do, including teaching, research, and service.<br><br></div><div>Drawing on our unique identity as the leading Hispanic-Serving Institution in a bilingual and bicultural environment, UTRGV will promote student access and success by building from strength in education and creating a vibrant campus experience. By 2027, we will accelerate transformation in the Rio Grande Valley and beyond by driving meaningful advancements in research and creative works, expanding access to high-quality and affordable healthcare, and fostering authentic community engagement and integration.<br><br></div><div>UTRGV is a distributed campus, one university spanning four counties and multiple locations. Our purpose is to be a university for the entire Rio Grande Valley and beyond. Over 91% of the students enrolled at UTRGV identify as Hispanic, making UTRGV one of the top 3 universities with the highest percentage of Hispanic students. For additional information, please visit <a href=\"https://www.utrgv.edu/index.htm\"><strong>UTRGV website</strong></a>.</div> RCV College of Business and Entrepreneurship / Marketing https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52115 2026-08-05T16:51:34-05:00 2026-08-05T16:51:35-05:00 ELECTRICIAN II <div>To provide journeyman level installation, maintenance, and service of electrical/electronic systems. Responsible for the safe and prompt performance of the maintenance, operation, repair and installation of electrical/electronic systems, fixtures, apparatus and equipment and other assigned duties.</div> Campus Facilities Operations https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52434 2026-09-02T15:22:21-05:00 2026-09-02T15:22:21-05:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant - EECE <div>Maximum appointment is limited to twenty (20) hours per week (50% FTE).</div> College of Engineering and Computer Science / Electrical and Computer Engineering https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51665 2026-06-30T10:08:58-05:00 2026-06-30T10:08:58-05:00 Assistant/Associate/Professor of Neurology <div>The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley (UTRGV) School of Medicine's Department of Neurology and Behavioral Health is seeking a full-time faculty member to serve as the Program Director of the newly founded Neurology Residency Program. The ideal candidate will continue the growth and sustainability of the residency program to include but not be limited to: teaching, further developing the Neurology residency with GME leaders, ISU Chair (according to ACGME accreditation requirements), leading didactics, sustaining and growing collaborative community partnerships in the Rio Grande Valley. Furthermore, the ideal candidate will provide outpatient care at UT Health’s Neurology Clinic located at the Institute of Neuroscience and potentially with other clinical partners with or without trainees.&nbsp;</div> School of Medicine / Neuro & Behavioral Health ISU https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52280 2026-08-19T15:29:31-05:00 2026-08-19T15:29:31-05:00 UNIVERSITY POLICE OFFICER IV - LAREDO <div>To enforce the law, provide service, information and aid to all citizens as circumstances require, prevent crime, suppress disturbances, investigate criminal offenses, and arrest offenders. Serves as a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). Responsible for enforcement duties for the protection, safety and welfare of students, employees, visitors, and all property within the area under the control and jurisdiction of The University of Texas System. Exercises independent judgment within the limits prescribed by law, Rules and Regulations of the Board of Regents, institutional rules and regulations and Director of Police departmental policies and procedures.</div> University Police"
