    "https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52449": {
      "title": "The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley Job Site | IT MEDIA SYSTEMS TECHNICIAN I",
      "description": "The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley Job Site | IT MEDIA SYSTEMS TECHNICIAN I Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Office Location The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley 1201 W. University Drive Human Resources MASS Building 2 nd Floor Edinburg, TX  78539 Edinburg: (956)665-2451 Brownsville: (956) 882-8205 Office hours: Monday-Friday 8:00a.m. - 5:00p.m. Staff Recruitment: careers@utrgv.edu School of Medicine Recruitment: SOMCareers@utrgv.edu Graduate Assistantships: assistantships@utrgv.edu Faculty Recruitment: College of Engineering & Computer Science: cecs@utrgv.edu Robert C. Vackar College of Business & Entrepreneurship: cobe@utrgv.edu College of Sciences Office of the Dean: cos@utrgv.edu College of Education and P-16 Integration: cep@utrgv.edu College of Fine Arts: cofa@utrgv.edu College of Liberal Arts: liberalarts@utrgv.edu Website: https://careers.utrgv.edu IT MEDIA SYSTEMS TECHNICIAN I Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: *Date of Birth *Gender *Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. If you have any questions, please visit our Careers site at https://careers.utrgv.edu for detailed contact information. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SRGV9134 Working Title IT MEDIA SYSTEMS TECHNICIAN I Number of Vacancies 1 Location Edinburg, Texas Department Infrastructure & Operations FTE 1 FLSA Non-Exempt Scope of Job To provide the daily operation, installation, troubleshooting, and maintenance of all assigned IT Media Systems, such as classroom technology systems, videoconferencing technology systems, and digital signage technology systems in support of UTRGV faculty, students, staff and visitors. Description of Duties • Provides daily operation, support and preventative maintenance of video networking infrastructure and activities (classes and conferences). • Performs routine installation, operation, troubleshooting, and maintenance on all assigned systems, including classroom technology systems, videoconferencing systems, computer-conferencing systems, special event media systems, digital signage systems and public address systems. • Performs hardware and software support for IT systems, including but not limited to computer systems, network monitoring systems, I.P. video recording systems, video networking systems, video cameras, microphones/mixers/amplifiers/speakers, projectors, monitors, and media recorders of various types. • Tests, troubleshoots, diagnoses and corrects IT Media Systems to ensure proper operations. • Installs and/or upgrades computer software and operating systems to ensure optimal performance. • Installs and/or upgrade classroom multimedia systems as required, ensuring optimal performance. • Keeps written records and reports of all activities and scheduled events • Manufactures audio/video/computer/control cables and connections as required for new installations/repairs. • Keeps up to date with information about evolving IT Media System trends for improvements of current systems (upgrades, best practices). • Makes recommendations for tools, equipment, office supplies, etc. for daily operations. • Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Received Specific supervision from assigned supervisor. Supervision Given Direct supervision of assigned support staff Required Education Associates Degree in Information Technology field, or 60 hours of College Credit with a minimum of 18 hours in IT related coursework. Preferred Education N/A Licenses/Certifications None. Required Experience • One (1) year of experience in technical support related to computer hardware, audio, video and computer equipment, multimedia display and control systems, networking and/or experience performing software upgrades, or • Three (3) years of the required experience with a High School Diploma or GED . Preferred Experience N/A Equipment Use of standard office equipment. Knowledge in hardware and software related to video, networking, audio/video/multimedia/presentation hardware and software installation, setup, and maintenance. Knowledge in conferencing technology operation and installation. Working Conditions Needs to be able to successfully perform all required duties, including setting up and connection of needed systems. Ability to lift equipment up to 30 pounds and perform work on ladders. Construction environment during installation projects along with office environment some travel and evening/weekend work is required. Other N/A Physical Capabilities N/A Employment Category Full-Time Minimum Salary Commensurate with Experience Posted Salary Commensurate with Experience Position Available Date 09/03/2026 Grant Funded Position No If Yes, Provide Grant Expiration Date Posting Detail Information EEO Statement It is the policy of The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley to promote and ensure equal employment opportunities for all individuals without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information or protected veteran status. In accordance with the requirements of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, as amended, our University is committed to comply with all government requirements and ensures non-discrimination in its education programs and activities, including employment. We encourage women, minorities and differently abled persons to apply for employment positions of interest. Special Instructions to Applicants Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: Date of Birth Gender *Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. If you have any questions, please visit our Careers site at https://careers.utrgv.edu for detailed contact information. Additional Information UTRGV is a distributed location institution and working location is subject to change based on need. All UTRGV employees are required to have a criminal background check ( CBC ). Incomplete applications will not be considered. Substitutions to the above requirements must have prior approval from the VP of HR & Talent Development . Quick Link https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52443 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UTRGV employee? Yes No * Are you now, or previously, employed by The University of Texas System or any of its institutions? Yes - I currently am employed by the UT System or its institutions Yes - I have previously been employed by the UT System or its institutions No - I have never been employed by the UT System or its institutions * Do you meet the minimum requirements for this position? Yes No * Please select your highest level of completed education. 6th grade education 10th grade education High School Diploma or GED Associates Degree, Technical, or Trade School Degree/Certification or 60 Hours of College Hours Bachelors Degree from an accredited university Masters Degree from an accredited university Ph. D. or other terminal degree from an accredited university None of the above * Please provide the field of study for your education: (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the number of years of work experience you have directly related to the position in which you are applying for: Less than 1 year 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years 6 years 7 years 8 years 9 years 10 years Over 10 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 Certifications and Licenses Training Certificates Other Document List of 3 References Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Letter of Interest Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Additional Document The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley UT System Employee Benefits UT System Fraud Reporting State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal Where the money goes To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
